    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="58cdc5fa-f902-4d80-b63e-d5f34c01d6b7">
      <data key="d3">The $400,000 face value of the policy is specifically assigned to Robert James Wilson as the insured party.</data>
      <data key="d4">assigned to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="38c15270-6db4-451e-bef6-7610864a498c">
      <data key="d3">The $400,000 death benefit establishes the policy’s financial value, which is sustained through regular payments like the minimum $75 monthly premium.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="97755915-52af-466c-a34e-6a2eda5319e2">
      <data key="d3">The $400,000 face value defines the total sum payable upon the insured’s death, which fully supports Jennifer Ann Wilson’s entitlement as the primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="f158b4b9-3d73-40b6-bbba-4bd340a2d7d2">
      <data key="d3">The $400,000 death benefit established in fact_sentence_1 serves as the basis for determining the portion received by Robert Wilson Jr. as a contingent beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="23a421cb-2b30-492b-90cc-7ef62985f8f6">
      <data key="d3">The policy's face value of $400,000 establishes the total death benefit available, which may be paid out to the contingent beneficiaries, Robert Wilson Jr. and Emily Rose Wilson, should the need arise.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="63e08fa1-6c41-4b13-8505-3af19ee3b242">
      <data key="d3">The $400,000 face value represents the total sum assured, which is paid out according to the Level (Option A) death benefit structure, ensuring a consistent payout regardless of when the claim occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="6ae0d7ce-3585-4c95-8412-49986f801824">
      <data key="d3">The $400,000 death benefit serves as the foundation for determining how much Emily Rose Wilson receives as a contingent beneficiary. Her entitlement of 50% depends on the existence and magnitude of the full policy value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="82af251d-d19c-45d0-95c3-15db9a931c70">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the $400,000 death benefit amount, which is consistent with Option A’s level payout structure confirmed in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8" target="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the $400,000 face value, which is validated by fact_sentence_2 stating that under Option A, the death benefit matches the specified amount exactly.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
