      <data key="d3">The Account Value depends on various deductions, one of which is the Cost of Insurance (COI). The COI represents a key charge used in calculating the net reduction of the Account Value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value depends on premium inputs, which are constrained by the annual cap mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49">
      <data key="d3">The Account Value depends on premium contributions meeting certain thresholds; without at least $75 per payment, the accumulation mechanism cannot function properly.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d3">The concept of Account Value depends on regular premium contributions, which are governed by flexible yet bounded payment rules outlined in the second sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value includes the impact of expense charges; thus, the process described in sentence 2—deducting a 3% fee before allocating premiums—is integral to how Account Value is calculated.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d3">The Account Value, defined as premiums less fees and augmented by interest, determines whether monthly deductions can be covered without additional payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The Account Value, defined as premiums minus fees and expenses plus interest, determines whether the policy can continue without interruption; if it drops too low, the system initiates a grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value establishes the financial foundation from which partial withdrawals are taken, making withdrawal capability contingent on its calculation and maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value provides foundational financial context relevant to understanding potential impacts of changing death benefits, such as increased premiums needed to support higher coverage levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value determines the upper limit for permissible partial withdrawals, ensuring policies remain in force after such transactions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d3">The Account Value, as defined in fact_sentence_1, represents the fund available for withdrawals; fact_sentence_2 sets a $500 floor on such withdrawals, limiting access to portions of the Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977">
      <data key="d3">The $25 withdrawal fee imposed in years 1–10 reduces the available Account Value, meaning each withdrawal diminishes the accumulated funds more significantly than just the withdrawn amount alone.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals decrease the Account Value by reducing the accumulated funds after premiums, fees, and interest have been applied.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value, as described in fact_sentence_1, determines the basis for the maximum allowable policy loan amount specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d3">The account value serves as collateral for policy loans, and the minimum loan interest rate of 4% determines the cost of borrowing against it, affecting overall policy economics.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">The account value grows based on premiums and interest, while the loan interest rate determines the cost of borrowing against that value, indirectly affecting future accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value depends on factors like interest crediting, while loan interest rates—which adjust annually—affect the cost of borrowing against that value, thereby influencing long-term account performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="733fa6c6-1173-4248-94bb-47741de40661">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value depends on accumulated funds less fees and charges; however, the surrender charge in year one further diminishes the amount received upon withdrawal, reducing the effective value realized.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">The account value serves as collateral for policy loans, which in turn directly reduce the death benefit. Thus, changes in account value due to premiums and fees influence the amount available for borrowing and ultimately affect the final death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The concept of Account Value defined in fact_sentence_1 serves as the foundational component used to calculate Cash Surrender Value, which is explicitly detailed in fact_sentence_2 after accounting for surrender charges and loan balances.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value includes monthly deductions like the $8.00 administrative charge described in fact_sentence_2, which reduces the accumulated value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value includes deductions such as the Cost of Insurance, which is explicitly charged monthly. Thus, fact_sentence_2 provides specific detail about one of the components shaping the calculation introduced in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">The dynamic nature of the annual interest rate impacts how quickly the Account Value grows over time, making it a key factor in determining its final accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value depends on periodic deductions, such as loan interest, which are explicitly outlined in fact_sentence_2 and fall under the broader category of "deductions" described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value relies on daily interest credits tied to an ongoing rate, which determines how much value accrues over time beyond premiums and fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The method of accumulating Account Value depends on interest credited, which may differ based on the account’s value level, adding complexity to growth predictions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value depends on interest credited, which is subject to a guaranteed minimum annual rate of 2.0%. This ensures a baseline return even if market rates fall below this threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">The current annual interest rate of 3.5% determines how much interest is credited to the Account Value, which directly impacts the accumulation formula defined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50">
      <data key="d3">The method by which Account Value grows relies on interest credited, which may differ across policy years, meaning fluctuations in these rates impact the total accumulated value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value impacts the potential growth and availability of funds used to support higher death benefit levels, particularly under an increasing option where the benefit includes account value. This makes the financial foundation relevant to modifying coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value depends on ongoing policy conditions, such as coverage level changes, which require evidence of insurability to ensure underwriting compliance before any adjustment occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda">
      <data key="d3">The $50 fee for changing death benefit options impacts the overall financial management of the account, influencing how much remains after transactions despite the primary accumulation method defined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value influences the final death benefit payment, which is adjusted downward by any unpaid policy loans, making the first fact foundational to assessing the second.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">Account Value serves as the base calculation for determining Cash Surrender Value, which adjusts it downward by surrender charges and any unpaid loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="d2bec389-f814-4532-8f19-68d9fc0c9d10">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value influences the final cash surrender value, which is reduced by the 8% surrender charge in Year 1, making it dependent on initial valuation metrics.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="be5a6946-58ba-4487-a91b-97d9949ba78f">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value, defined in fact_sentence_1, determines the base figure used to compute the cash surrender value, which includes the 5% surrender charge specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value provides the foundation for determining the payout upon policy surrender, which terminates coverage as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed">
      <data key="d3">The Account Value, as defined by fact_sentence_1, serves as the base figure from which surrender charges are subtracted. In Year 10, a 2% surrender charge applies, reducing the actual return an owner receives when terminating the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="f6b5e972-2fde-453a-98fa-9ea8711ed5fa">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value depends on ongoing fee structures, but by Year 15, surrender charges vanish, allowing full access to the accumulated Account Value without penalty.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value provides the basis for determining the payout upon surrender, making it central to understanding the outcome described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value depends on accurate disclosures at issuance; if misrepresentations exist, the insurer may invalidate the policy before it fully vests its benefits, potentially nullifying the accrued value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value establishes the basis for determining the payout amount if the insured dies by suicide within two years, ensuring clarity on what portion of the policy's value is disbursed under such circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the standard calculation of Account Value, while fact_sentence_2 specifies an exception where no interest is credited if suicide occurs within two years, thereby limiting the growth potential of the Account Value at payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="64f378fd-3e2e-4610-87e4-f7c8a0139286">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Account Value provides the financial basis for potential payouts, which may be subject to contestation under the two-year rule described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">If the Account Value cannot cover monthly deductions, the policy continues for up to 61 days without interruption, allowing time to restore funds before lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of Account Value determines whether the policy remains active during the 61-day grace period; insufficient funds may lead to lapse if unaddressed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">Understanding how Account Value is computed allows one to assess whether it exceeds surrender charges upon policy lapse, determining the amount返还 to the policyholder.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0e782201-7763-48dc-9079-65f63b0ad297" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is defined as</data>
    </edge>
