    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance (COI) is a monthly fee applied to reduce the Account Value; its amount influences how much remains after premium deposits and interest crediting.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="db29af61-a32c-4cab-b447-68c30c95049a">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance is a monthly fee that contributes to overall deductions, potentially occurring on the 10th of each month if applicable.</data>
      <data key="d4">occurs on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance (COI) contributes to the monthly deductions from the account. As long as the account has sufficient value to cover these deductions—including COI—payments may be skipped without lapsing coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance (COI) determines the monthly cost of maintaining the death benefit, while flexible premium payments allow policyholders to adjust contributions within set bounds. Adequate premiums ensure continuous coverage, indirectly supporting sustained COI application over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance (COI) is a key component of the monthly charges that reduce the account value. When the account value declines due to such charges—including COI—it may drop below the minimum required level, triggering the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance (COI) depends on personal risk factors and contributes to overall policy costs alongside the fixed administrative fee mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary charges</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">The first fact defines what the Cost of Insurance (COI) is, while the second clarifies that it is deducted monthly from the Account Value, showing how the defined charge is implemented operationally.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance (COI) is a recurring monthly charge applied to maintain coverage, which occurs alongside the deduction of policy loan interest from the Account Value on the same date. Together, these deductions impact the overall account balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance impacts the account value, which serves as the base for daily interest calculations. While COI deducts funds periodically, interest credits help offset these reductions over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance directly influences the policyholder’s out-of-pocket costs, which may indirectly affect how much funds remain available for investment returns driven by fluctuating interest rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">independently relevant</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance depends on underwriting factors, while the guaranteed minimum interest rate ensures a baseline return on the account value, influencing long-term sustainability of coverage despite COI charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance depends on personal risk factors, while the 3.5% annual interest rate determines growth potential of the account value. Together, they shape the total cost and return profile of the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">independently relevant</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance influences the net return on the policy’s account value, while fluctuating credited interest rates impact how much the account grows over time. Together, they shape the long-term economic viability of the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance impacts the account value, which may influence the applicable credited interest rate based on account size. This creates an indirect link where financial dynamics governed by COI contribute to conditions under which variable interest rates might be applied.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences indirectly</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability when increasing coverage relies on the underlying cost-of-insurance model, which determines pricing based on risk profile.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance depends on the chosen death benefit option, so changing these options affects the COI charged monthly. This implies that adjustments to the death benefit require recalculating the COI based on updated risk parameters.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance impacts the accumulation of account value, which indirectly determines available funds to offset policy loans before death benefit payment. This creates a dependency where higher COI reduces surplus value, limiting cushion against loan liabilities.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
