    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">To generate an Account Value as defined by the formula, a minimum premium of $75 must be paid, ensuring eligibility for inclusion in the accumulation process.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d3">The requirement of a $75 minimum payment sets a foundational constraint that ensures compliance with the flexible premium system outlined in the second sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83">
      <data key="d3">The minimum $75 payment ensures that each contribution meets a baseline threshold, while the maximum $50,000 annual cap prevents excessive deposits that could trigger tax penalties or violate policy guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The minimum $75 payment ensures eligibility for premium processing; without meeting this threshold, the subsequent deduction of a 3% expense charge would not occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Insufficient premium payments, such as those falling below the $75 minimum, may reduce the Account Value to a point where it cannot sustain monthly charges, leading to the initiation of a 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that each payment be at least $75 ensures sufficient funding capacity, enabling the account to sustain operations even if future payments are skipped, assuming the Account Value remains adequate.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="38c15270-6db4-451e-bef6-7610864a498c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes a baseline requirement of $75 per payment, which is explicitly confirmed and contextualized by fact_sentence_1 in relation to a specific policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="c7b13fca-a0cc-4be7-b051-d4ce5ea2b5ca">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a $75 minimum premium supports the feasibility of the $200 planned premium, confirming it meets the lower threshold set by the policy guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="23a421cb-2b30-492b-90cc-7ef62985f8f6">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for a $75 minimum premium ensures the policy remains active, thereby preserving the intended distribution of benefits to contingent beneficiaries Robert Wilson Jr. and Emily Rose Wilson.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="f158b4b9-3d73-40b6-bbba-4bd340a2d7d2">
      <data key="d3">The $75 minimum premium ensures the policy remains active, enabling the contingency plan where Robert Wilson Jr. can receive his 50% portion of the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="6ae0d7ce-3585-4c95-8412-49986f801824">
      <data key="d3">The $75 minimum premium ensures the policy remains active, enabling the fulfillment of beneficiary payouts such as Emily Rose Wilson’s 50% share of the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49" target="63e08fa1-6c41-4b13-8505-3af19ee3b242">
      <data key="d3">The mandatory $75 minimum premium supports the maintenance of the Level (Option A) death benefit, ensuring the policy remains active and the promised payout is preserved.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f1724dcb-a626-46e6-9e0e-7f70c51dcc34" target="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49">
