      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83" target="dc2efefb-7ca6-4c09-916a-cd536325acd7">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium limit affects how much can contribute to increasing the Account Value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83" target="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49">
      <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual ceiling provides context for why a $75 minimum exists—payments must stay within a defined band to remain compliant with both internal policy rules and external tax laws.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual cap ensures compliance with IRS tax rules, defining the outer limit within which flexible premium payments operate under the policy's guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium cap ensures that contributions remain within IRS limits, enabling the account to accumulate enough value so that future payments can potentially be skipped without triggering lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium limit of $50,000 constrains the total amount eligible for deposit into the account, thereby influencing the pre-deduction pool used to calculate the 3% expense charge applied under the policy’s funding rules.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Higher premium amounts constrained by the $50,000 annual limit could reduce the likelihood of falling below the minimum Account Value needed to cover monthly charges, thereby decreasing the chance of triggering the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2b518a2f-25c4-47c5-976a-5e1a98da0e85" target="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has limit</data>
    </edge>
