      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="383d8d5b-4aa1-461a-b4cb-97994a459fff">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="36f4cb0a-0972-4e42-9cc8-d556f993ea85">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Flexible premium payment options allow for consistent funding of the Account Value, ensuring ongoing accumulation as defined in the first sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">Flexible premium payments enable adjustments in contribution amounts within specified limits, ensuring sufficient funds exist to cover ongoing costs such as the Cost of Insurance (COI), which is calculated based on individual risk profiles.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables payment</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49">
      <data key="d3">The allowance for variable premium timing and amounts depends on meeting the $75 minimum, making the first fact a necessary condition for applying the second.</data>
      <data key="d4">enforces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83">
      <data key="d3">Flexible premium payments are constrained by the $50,000 yearly maximum imposed by tax regulations, ensuring adherence to legal thresholds.</data>
      <data key="d4">bound by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The ability to make flexible premium payments sets the stage for the subsequent application of the 3% expense charge. After a payment is made within allowable limits, the deduction occurs before allocation to the Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d3">The allowance for flexible premium payments enables policyholders to skip contributions as long as the existing Account Value remains sufficient to cover required monthly deductions without lapsing coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Flexible premium payments allow policyholders to maintain sufficient Account Value; if payments are inadequate, the account may fall short of covering monthly charges, triggering the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents grace period</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a83e0d16-5c54-4983-a368-b7d3389d6a19" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has flexible premium payment</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d5cc9aa1-4eb2-463a-99a8-8dd4e458b0f7" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has flexible premium payment</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="776f3a56-b2cc-4d1a-a581-7c9661d173e4" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">increases with premium payment</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a01ce58-07d7-4f27-83ff-e2e012341da9" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">associated with premium payment cycle</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="edd8ca1e-7f50-45cf-8e9b-7f2ab5fbf7a0" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">sets lower limit on premium payment</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="68d693a7-c924-411e-9a39-2dfd500a6664" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">sets lower limit on premium payment</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="9fb60615-cc44-4098-89ee-eb56e07c6f63">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">person</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="41478754-5d77-4322-8ba1-903605bb48aa">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">person</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="a1d95120-7ed4-4191-a343-d9eff1211454">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="272b16bf-fe47-47c4-b321-8e0edde82f0c">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="291882bc-517f-467b-9a59-a9807aaca55f">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="4acf9dff-a5c0-441e-8814-70a9647dc7be">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="15bc54f5-a1dc-495a-af92-84b42a515235">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="14dcc6c6-179e-41d0-9d15-b74e44bac016">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="ebd53904-1bc1-4d99-8e87-c9518fa2d511">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="5fe455ae-225b-4c7c-a3ef-4b61f5b565ac">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Premiums are added to the Account Value only after a 3% expense charge is subtracted, making this allocation rule necessary for accurately determining the Account Value as defined earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="db29af61-a32c-4cab-b447-68c30c95049a">
      <data key="d3">Premiums are processed according to the 3% expense charge only after the Monthly Deduction Date has passed, ensuring timely allocation based on scheduled billing cycles.</data>
      <data key="d4">after</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49">
      <data key="d3">Once a payment meets or exceeds $75, the system deducts a 3% expense charge from the amount before allocating the remainder to Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83">
      <data key="d3">The 3% expense charge deducted from each premium payment depends on the actual amount contributed; therefore, the existence of a $50,000 annual ceiling ensures that no more than this figure can trigger such a deduction annually.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d3">Payments must first comply with the specified limits and timing rules before the 3% expense charge applies; thus, the processing step relies directly on prior compliance with payment conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to Account Value after a 3% fee enables the account to sustain itself over time, allowing it to support skipped payments when balances remain sufficient.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The deduction of a 3% expense charge on premiums reduces the Account Value over time. If repeated or combined with other withdrawals, this reduction may cause the Account Value to fall below the threshold needed to sustain monthly charges, triggering the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="38c15270-6db4-451e-bef6-7610864a498c">
      <data key="d3">The 3% expense charge applied to premiums depends on meeting the minimum $75 monthly requirement, ensuring sufficient funds remain for account buildup despite fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="c7b13fca-a0cc-4be7-b051-d4ce5ea2b5ca">
      <data key="d3">The processing rule in fact_sentence_2—that 3% of each premium is deducted before allocation—directly applies to the $200 monthly premium mentioned in fact_sentence_1, determining its effective contribution to the policy’s account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains mechanism</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="23a421cb-2b30-492b-90cc-7ef62985f8f6">
      <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 describes how premiums contribute to the Account Value after a 3% fee, this mechanism indirectly supports the long-term viability of the death benefit paid to the beneficiaries mentioned in fact_sentence_1, though it doesn't affect their identity or share.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables outcome</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="6ae0d7ce-3585-4c95-8412-49986f801824">
      <data key="d3">The mechanism by which premiums contribute to the Account Value affects long-term policy performance, indirectly influencing whether sufficient funds exist to pay out the full death benefit to Emily as a contingent beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="63e08fa1-6c41-4b13-8505-3af19ee3b242">
      <data key="d3">The 3% premium expense charge impacts the growth of the Account Value, which indirectly sustains the ability to fulfill the promised Level (Option A) death benefit throughout the policy term.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d3">The processing of premiums into the Account Value affects overall policy value, which may influence decisions regarding higher death benefits requiring evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d3">The accumulation of Account Value via premium deposits—after a 3% expense deduction—is foundational to enabling future partial withdrawals. Without this process, there would be no account value available for withdrawal.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after a 3% deduction; subsequent partial withdrawals further decrease this value, affecting its growth trajectory.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after a 3% deduction, forming the basis from which partial withdrawals may be made; thus, the availability of sufficient Account Value due to proper premium allocation enables compliance with the $500 minimum withdrawal requirement.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">The premium allocation rule directly influences the Account Value, which sets the upper limit for permissible partial withdrawals under the policy's maintenance requirements.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after an initial deduction, forming the basis for potential withdrawals; however, withdrawals within the first decade are subject to a $25 fee, adding cost to accessing funds built from those premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to the Account Value after a 3% deduction enables the growth of funds that subsequently determine the maximum allowable policy loan, which is capped at 90% of that value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">The method by which premiums increase the Account Value indirectly supports the availability of funds used for policy loans, which subsequently reduce the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to Account Value after a 3% fee sets the basis for determining the Account Value, which is a key factor in computing the Cash Surrender Value as defined in the second statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="733fa6c6-1173-4248-94bb-47741de40661">
      <data key="d3">The 3% premium expense charge reduces the amount added to the Account Value initially, while the 8% surrender charge in year one affects the final payout if the policy is terminated early. Together, these fees impact long-term accumulation and potential returns.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary cost</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">The initial premium allocation is reduced by a fixed percentage upfront, and later, recurring costs like the Cost of Insurance are deducted monthly, cumulatively impacting the Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">The 3% premium expense charge reduces incoming funds before they enter the Account Value, which later becomes subject to the $8.00 monthly administrative deduction. Together, these charges progressively diminish the growth potential of the Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary charges</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after an initial fee, which may influence the total fund available before monthly deductions like loan interest occur. The timing and order of these transactions suggest potential cumulative impact on account balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The initial allocation of premiums to the Account Value after fees establishes the foundation upon which daily interest is calculated, linking funding to growth mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">Premiums are initially reduced by a 3% fee before being added to the Account Value, which then earns interest based on a variable annual rate that can change monthly.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after a 3% fee, which then earns interest at an annual rate of 3.5%, influencing long-term growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">Premiums deposited into the account are reduced by a 3% fee before being added to the Account Value, which then earns interest at an annual rate that is guaranteed not to fall below 2.0%. This ensures stable growth even if market rates decline.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The processing of premiums into the Account Value after an expense charge sets the foundation for future growth, which could be influenced by differing interest rates applied depending on the account's size.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to the Account Value affects the total fund available before deducting outstanding policy loans, which directly influences the final death benefit paid out.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">Premiums increase the Account Value after a 3% fee, which directly contributes to determining the Cash Surrender Value by forming its base amount before deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="be5a6946-58ba-4487-a91b-97d9949ba78f">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after a 3% fee, influencing the total funds available before any future surrender charges like the 5% fee in Year 5 are applied.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="d2bec389-f814-4532-8f19-68d9fc0c9d10">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after a 3% fee, which influences the total amount available before any future surrender charges are applied. The 8% surrender charge in Year 1 reduces the net payout if the policy is terminated early, potentially affecting returns from accumulated funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after a 3% fee, which influences the amount available before applying later surrender charges like the 2% fee in Year 10.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to the Account Value after expenses enables the buildup of funds that determine the cash surrender value, which triggers policy termination upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="f6b5e972-2fde-453a-98fa-9ea8711ed5fa">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after a 3% fee, influencing the total funds available at surrender. By year 15, surrender charges drop to zero, allowing full access to accumulated value without penalty.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">Premiums contribute to the Account Value after expenses, building the foundation for potential future surrender benefits; however, surrendering the policy ultimately ends coverage regardless of accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">The allocation method described in fact_sentence_1 determines the size of the Account Value that becomes relevant in determining payouts under the conditions specified in fact_sentence_2, particularly regarding suicide-related benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20">
      <data key="d3">The premium allocation rule applies regardless of potential future contests due to misrepresentation, meaning that even if the policy is challenged later, initial premium processing still occurs under standard fee structures.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">The initial allocation of premiums to the Account Value after expenses determines the basis for calculating surplus funds that may be returned upon policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">The allocation method for premiums affects the Account Value level, directly influencing whether monthly deductions can be sustained. When the Account Value falls below required levels due to expenses, the 61-day grace period activates.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums after a 3% deduction directly affects whether sufficient funds are available to prevent lapse within the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a1d95120-7ed4-4191-a343-d9eff1211454" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">receives</data>
    </edge>
