      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="50e84c85-aeb6-4468-a00b-d9f07c648515">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The ability to skip payments relies on having an adequate Account Value, which is itself determined by prior contributions, fees, and accrued interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">If the account holds adequate value to meet monthly deductions such as the cost of insurance (COI), payment skips become permissible, ensuring continued policy validity despite nonpayment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="db29af61-a32c-4cab-b447-68c30c95049a">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 relies on the existence of a defined monthly deduction schedule—established by fact sentence 1—to determine eligibility for skipping payments. Without a set deduction date, the conditionality around fund sufficiency would lack temporal context.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49">
      <data key="d3">If an account has built up enough value through previous contributions—including those meeting the $75 minimum—it can afford to skip a payment without triggering lapses due to insufficient funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83">
      <data key="d3">If the Account Value stays above required levels after monthly deductions, it allows flexibility to skip premium payments, making the annual limit less restrictive in practice.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d3">The possibility of skipping payments relies on prior permission granted by flexible premium rules, which permit varying payment schedules and amounts under specified limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The possibility of skipping payments hinges on maintaining enough Account Value, which is directly influenced by how premiums are initially allocated post-expense deduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">When the Account Value remains high enough to cover monthly deductions, payments may be skipped without penalty. However, if it drops below the necessary amount, the policy activates a 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5143034b-ef00-438d-97d5-6e8b35c3bcc3" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">enables payment skip</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cff3fc01-ea1f-4cc2-9cba-fac622d5f060" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is deducted monthly</data>
    </edge>
