      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">A drop in Account Value below the threshold needed to cover monthly charges activates a 61-day grace period, highlighting that the Account Value’s maintenance relies on its calculated components.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">When the account value becomes insufficient to cover ongoing costs like the cost of insurance (COI), the policy triggers a 61-day grace period, signaling that expenses such as COI have contributed to depleting reserves.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="db29af61-a32c-4cab-b447-68c30c95049a">
      <data key="d3">When the Account Value becomes too low to sustain monthly charges, it initiates the 61-day grace period. Since the monthly deduction happens on the 10th, this event depends on the prior occurrence of the deduction date.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="bf17bd2f-cc01-4aed-ab90-14364c05da49">
      <data key="d3">The occurrence of a 61-day grace period due to inadequate Account Value implies that prior premium payments might have been too low or infrequent, potentially violating the $75 minimum requirement.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="74a711a2-97b3-4f95-aa04-0a96095d0a83">
      <data key="d3">The possibility of entering a 61-day grace period arises when the Account Value fails to meet monthly charge requirements, which underscores why controlling premium inputs within the $50,000 annual ceiling is critical to maintaining sufficient fund levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="df4d1d6e-8a2e-4aef-be1d-f03f2bb2dee0">
      <data key="d3">When the Account Value drops too low to cover monthly charges, it indicates that prior premium payments were either delayed or insufficient, highlighting the importance of meeting payment limits as outlined earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on payments</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="59fb32e1-012d-434e-b8c3-5bdbc033f263">
      <data key="d3">A drop in Account Value below the minimum needed for monthly charges initiates a 61-day grace period. During this time, payment skips become permissible until funds recover or coverage lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">When the Account Value drops too low to cover monthly charges, the policy enters a 61-day grace period. This situation arises because prior premium allocations were diminished by the 3% expense charge, reducing overall fund growth and increasing vulnerability to insufficiency.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d3">A drop in Account Value leading to a grace period may result from frequent or large partial withdrawals, suggesting that such actions can trigger the condition outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">can trigger</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977">
      <data key="d3">A reduction in Account Value due to withdrawal fees during the first ten years may cause the account to fall below the threshold needed to cover monthly charges, thereby triggering the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">A high partial withdrawal might deplete the Account Value below the required level, potentially initiating the 61-day grace period outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d3">A low Account Value triggering the 61-day grace period may result from excessive partial withdrawals; since the minimum withdrawal is $500, frequent or large withdrawals could deplete the account faster, risking entry into the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">A decrease in Account Value due to partial withdrawals raises the likelihood of falling below the required level for monthly charges, potentially activating the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">A drop in Account Value triggering the 61-day grace period may lead policyholders to utilize policy loans, which are capped at 90% of the Account Value, as a means to sustain coverage temporarily.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">A policy loan reduces the account value, which may cause it to fall below the threshold needed to cover monthly charges, thereby activating the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The grace period condition hinges on sufficient Account Value, which is reduced by outstanding loans and surrender charges as specified in the second fact, thus influencing whether the policy avoids lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to deduct the Cost of Insurance monthly can cause the Account Value to fall below the necessary threshold, thereby initiating the 61-day grace period outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">The $8.00 monthly administrative charge reduces the Account Value, potentially causing it to fall below the required level and triggering the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The grace period starts when Account Value cannot cover monthly charges, which may result from deductions like loan interest. Loan interest being deducted monthly increases pressure on the Account Value, making it more likely to fall below the required threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">A fluctuating annual interest rate impacts the accumulation of account value, thereby influencing whether the account stays above the threshold needed to avoid initiating a 61-day grace period due to insufficient funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows time to restore account value without immediate lapse, during which daily interest accrual helps rebuild funds toward meeting payment thresholds.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">A lower guaranteed interest rate could increase the risk of the account value falling below the threshold needed to cover charges, thereby making the 61-day grace period more likely. This creates an indirect dependency where the minimum interest rate helps sustain sufficient account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50">
      <data key="d3">A lower credited interest rate could slow account value accumulation, increasing the risk that it falls below the threshold needed to cover monthly charges, thereby triggering the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">A higher interest rate like 3.5% helps maintain or increase the account value over time, reducing the risk that it will fall below the required level to cover monthly charges, thereby decreasing the chance of triggering the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly related</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The grace period depends on account value stability, which can be influenced by variable interest rates applied differently across account balances, affecting whether the value stays sufficient to avoid triggering the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">A drop in account value triggering a grace period can lead to accumulating debt via unpaid charges and loan interest, directly impacting the net death benefit available after deducting outstanding loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="d2bec389-f814-4532-8f19-68d9fc0c9d10">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows temporary continuation of coverage despite insufficient funds, potentially delaying surrender decisions that would incur an 8% surrender charge in year one.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">When the Account Value drops too low, initiating a 61-day grace period, the resulting Cash Surrender Value becomes critical if the policy is surrendered before lapse, since it reflects net recoverable value after deducting charges and loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows time to address insufficient funds, potentially enabling policyholders to choose surrender before lapse occurs, linking financial status to termination options.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows time to address insufficient funds, during which the policyholder may choose to surrender the policy, thereby ending coverage prematurely rather than waiting for lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">allows surrender</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">A drop in Account Value triggering a 61-day grace period may precede a suicide-related claim within the two-year contestability window, affecting whether full death benefits are paid or only the Account Value is disbursed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains the trigger for the 61-day grace period due to inadequate Account Value, which directly supports fact_sentence_2’s assertion that the policy remains active during this window.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">When the account value falls short of covering monthly charges, a 61-day grace period begins, allowing time to make up the deficit. If insufficient premium isn’t received within this timeframe, the policy ultimately lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">When the account value drops too low, triggering a 61-day grace period, it sets up the condition under which the policy may eventually lapse, leading to automatic payout of surplus account value after surrender charges are subtracted.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
