      <data key="d3">The Monthly Deduction Date triggers financial adjustments within the policy. On this date, the Cost of Insurance charge is specifically subtracted from the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence states that deductions happen monthly on a set date. The second clarifies that one such deduction is a fixed $8.00 administrative fee charged on that same date.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The monthly deduction event provides the context for when loan interest is subtracted from the account value. Loan interest is processed specifically during the regular monthly deduction cycle.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="cfdb2248-6b51-4750-aa82-60cc46963f85">
      <data key="d3">The regular monthly deduction is supported by the guaranteed limits on COI rates, ensuring predictable costs over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="d8801d10-4c5d-4ab8-88e5-7f8a5417a886">
      <data key="d3">The monthly deduction event described in sentence 1 includes the Cost of Insurance charge, which is computed using the specified formula involving the difference between the Specified Amount and Account Value, adjusted by the Monthly COI Rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The monthly deduction event depends on the accumulation of daily interest, which influences the account balance used to determine the deduction amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions occur regularly based on policy terms, and the guaranteed minimum interest rate ensures a baseline return used in calculating such deductions over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions depend on the prevailing interest rate, which can vary each month. Therefore, changes in the interest rate impact the amount deducted during each monthly cycle.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions occur regularly according to schedule, while differing interest rates per policy year affect how much interest accumulates over time, influencing the net effect of each deduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The monthly deduction depends on factors like account value, which determines the applicable interest rate used in calculations. This implies that differing interest rates for various account sizes influence the deduction’s final amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions affect the account value, which contributes to determining the death benefit under Option B. This means the ongoing charges indirectly shape the total payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions occur regularly and may impact the account balance used to settle outstanding loans. These reductions influence the net death benefit payment, which is adjusted downward if loans remain unpaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="63e08fa1-6c41-4b13-8505-3af19ee3b242">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions ensure the financial stability necessary to uphold the promised level death benefit, making them essential to sustaining the benefit choice.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="c7b13fca-a0cc-4be7-b051-d4ce5ea2b5ca">
      <data key="d3">Regular monthly deductions, as mentioned in fact_sentence_2, include the $200 premium stated in fact_sentence_1, forming part of the essential payments that sustain the policy’s active status.</data>
      <data key="d4">funding source</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="38c15270-6db4-451e-bef6-7610864a498c">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions include essential charges such as cost of insurance and administration fees, making it necessary to meet the $75 minimum premium to avoid policy lapse due to insufficient funding.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9" target="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions impact the policy’s account balance, influencing whether sufficient funds remain to maintain the $400,000 death benefit promised in the first fact.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
