    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9">
      <data key="d3">The deduction of the Cost of Insurance charge only takes place if the Monthly Deduction Date has occurred, making the timing of the charge contingent upon this scheduled date.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance charge is subtracted from the account value monthly, similar to how the Administrative expense charge is applied. Both are recurring deductions that occur simultaneously during the monthly cycle.</data>
      <data key="d4">simultaneously deducted</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance charge is subtracted from the account value monthly, independent of other deductions like loan interest. This ensures consistent coverage costs regardless of borrowing activity.</data>
      <data key="d4">co occurs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="cfdb2248-6b51-4750-aa82-60cc46963f85">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance (COI) charge is deducted monthly based on the policy’s terms, but its amount is constrained by pre-specified rates outlined in the attached schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="d8801d10-4c5d-4ab8-88e5-7f8a5417a886">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance charge is deducted monthly from the account value based on a specific calculation involving the difference between the specified amount and the account value, adjusted by the monthly rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of the Cost of Insurance impacts the Account Value, which is defined in fact_sentence_1 as being reduced by various charges—including this one—over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">The second fact describes the timing and method of deduction for the Cost of Insurance, which depends entirely on the definition provided in the first fact regarding its nature and basis.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions such as the Cost of Insurance affect the Account Value, which was initially built up from premiums after a 3% expense deduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows time to restore sufficient Account Value after ongoing deductions like the Cost of Insurance, preventing immediate lapse despite insufficient funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers grace period</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="63e08fa1-6c41-4b13-8505-3af19ee3b242">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions such as the Cost of Insurance affect the account value over time, yet do not impact the chosen level death benefit structure already established in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">independent support</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="c7b13fca-a0cc-4be7-b051-d4ce5ea2b5ca">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance charge being deducted from the account value depends on consistent premium payments, such as the $200 monthly contribution, to maintain sufficient funding.</data>
      <data key="d4">funding source</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="38c15270-6db4-451e-bef6-7610864a498c">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance charge being deducted from the account value depends on having adequate premium payments, making the $75 minimum premium necessary to support these ongoing deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance charge impacts the Account Value, which directly influences the Cash Surrender Value calculated under fact_sentence_2. Higher recurring charges may lower the Account Value, thereby reducing potential surrender proceeds.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8">
      <data key="d3">Monthly deductions like the Cost of Insurance impact the account value, which may affect the ability to sustain the $400,000 death benefit if insufficient reserves accumulate, though the face value remains unchanged unless altered via official modification.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="be5a6946-58ba-4487-a91b-97d9949ba78f">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance charge reduces the account value monthly, while the Year 5 surrender charge is applied only if the policy is terminated, reducing the final payout. These charges affect the same underlying asset pool differently—one periodic, the other contingent on surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">The monthly Cost of Insurance charge ceases upon policy surrender, meaning continued deductions depend on the policy remaining active.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of the cost of insurance maintains active coverage, but upon surrender, even if payments continue, the policy ends and benefits cease.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance deduction affects the account value that may later be paid out upon death, including in cases of suicide within two years. This means ongoing charges could reduce the final account value available for such a payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d">
      <data key="d3">When the Cost of Insurance charge exceeds available Account Value, the insurer notifies the policyholder, ensuring awareness before potential lapse due to non-payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance deduction occurs regularly regardless of claim events, but if the insured dies by suicide within 24 months, no interest accrues on the Account Value used for the payout, effectively reducing its final value despite ongoing deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional exclusion</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance charge is regularly deducted from the Account Value, but if funds are insufficient, the policy continues for up to 61 days without lapse, allowing time to resolve shortfalls.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of the cost of insurance reduces the account value over time, directly affecting the amount available for automatic payout upon policy lapse, as described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">The monthly cost of insurance deduction relies on consistent premium inflows; if premiums are not paid timely, the policy risks lapsing before these deductions can continue effectively.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
