    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate enables the precise computation of loan interest, which is subsequently deducted from the account value on the Monthly Deduction Date.</data>
      <data key="d4">drives</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="267656a2-1874-42ab-acb1-f06594a6ea4e">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate enables the daily crediting of interest to the account value, forming the mechanism through which growth occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The stated annual interest rate of 3.5% serves as the basis for calculating daily interest credits on the policy’s account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">The current annual interest rate of 3.5% reflects the active crediting rate being applied now, which surpasses the guaranteed minimum of 2%, ensuring higher returns under prevailing conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">exceeds minimum</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">The current interest rate of 3.5% may fluctuate monthly, meaning it is not guaranteed to remain constant over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The current 3.5% annual interest rate applies under general terms but may differ based on individual account value levels, suggesting tiered crediting.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50">
      <data key="d3">The stated current rate of 3.5% per annum exemplifies how credited interest rates may differ across policy years, illustrating one possible value within an expected range of variations.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">The current interest rate of 3.5% affects the growth of the account value over time, which contributes to the total death benefit under Option B.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The method by which Account Value grows—including interest crediting—is dependent on the stated annual interest rate of 3.5%, which validates the mechanics described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% interest rate enhances the accumulation of account value, which can offset some of the ongoing cost of insurance charges, helping maintain policy viability despite recurring COI deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">A 3.5% annual interest rate applies to funds accumulated via premiums, which are first reduced by a 3% expense charge before being invested.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period exists precisely because the account value may decline due to fees and charges; however, the ongoing accrual of interest at 3.5% annually supports recovery, helping prevent permanent lapse despite temporary shortfalls.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly related</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate impacts the account value, which is a key component in calculating the cash surrender value described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate contributes to growing the account value, which forms part of the cash surrender value when the policy is terminated under fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="f6b5e972-2fde-453a-98fa-9ea8711ed5fa">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate contributes to growing the account value over time, directly impacting the cash surrender value available after Year 15 when surrender charges drop to zero.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="be5a6946-58ba-4487-a91b-97d9949ba78f">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate contributes to growing the account value over time, which indirectly affects the cash surrender value used to calculate the net return after subtracting the 5% surrender charge in Year 5.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate contributes to growing the account value, which determines the cash surrender value when coverage ends upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate affects the accumulation of the account value, which determines the payout amount if the insured dies by suicide within two years, as stipulated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate normally increases the account value, but it is explicitly excluded if the insured dies by suicide within the first two years, meaning no interest accrues on the payout in such cases.</data>
      <data key="d4">exception to rule</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d">
      <data key="d3">A higher interest rate like 3.5% helps maintain or grow the account value, reducing the risk that it becomes insufficient to cover monthly deductions, thereby lowering the chance of a notification being sent.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">A 3.5% annual interest rate helps grow the account value, reducing the risk that it becomes insufficient to cover monthly deductions, thereby lowering the chance of activating the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">The 3.5% annual interest rate contributes to growing the account value, which increases the potential amount refunded to the policyholder upon lapse, assuming it exceeds surrender charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
