      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">option</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="355e6de6-345b-4d9d-949c-95d8d6c7c964">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">condition</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="0634ab99-6117-4be2-b372-18f5c24e5708">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">charge</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="82f899ed-d5e6-45cf-8b76-d1f3308b76d8">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">benefit</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9">
      <data key="d3">Since deductions happen every month, any adjustment to the interest rate has immediate implications for the deduction calculations performed on the Monthly Deduction Date.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The monthly adjustment of the interest rate affects how much loan interest accumulates, thereby influencing the amount subtracted from the account value during each monthly deduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="267656a2-1874-42ab-acb1-f06594a6ea4e">
      <data key="d3">Monthly adjustments to the interest rate directly impact the daily calculation of interest credited to the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">Changes to the monthly interest rate affect how daily interest is computed, influencing the actual credit amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">The current interest rate may adjust monthly but remains bounded above by market conditions and constrained below by the 2.0% guarantee established in the prior statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">bound by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">Because the interest rate can change monthly, the currently reported rate of 3.5% reflects only a temporary state and could differ in subsequent periods.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50">
      <data key="d3">The potential for monthly adjustments in the interest rate enables variations in credited rates across different policy years, making such differences plausible and consistent with dynamic rate management.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The potential for monthly fluctuations in the interest rate complements the possibility of differing rates applied according to account value levels, allowing for dynamic adjustments based on both timing and individual account characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d4">variables within framework</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">The fluctuating annual interest rate affects the accumulation of account value over time, which contributes to the total death benefit under Option B. However, the statement about the interest rate changing monthly does not directly influence the formulaic definition of the increasing death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The method by which Account Value increases relies heavily on the interest rate being applied, so any variation in the rate directly influences the accuracy and outcome of the valuation process outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">Fluctuations in the annual interest rate impact how quickly the account value grows, thereby influencing whether sufficient funds are available to cover ongoing cost of insurance charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">independently relevant</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">A fluctuating annual interest rate impacts the growth of the Account Value, which is influenced by how premiums are allocated post-expense deduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Changes in the annual interest rate may accelerate or slow down the decline of account value, affecting the timing and probability of falling below the required level that triggers a 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">The variable interest rate impacts the account value, which is a core factor in calculating the cash surrender value described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">Changes in the monthly interest rate impact the account value, which determines the cash surrender value upon policy termination. Therefore, the dynamic interest rate influences the financial outcome when the policy is surrendered.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">The fluctuating interest rate affects the account value used to calculate the cash surrender value, influencing the payout upon policy termination. Thus, while the rate itself doesn’t cause surrender, it shapes the financial result when coverage ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences outcome</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">The account value referenced in the suicide payout rule is affected by the monthly-changing interest rate, meaning fluctuations in the rate impact the final payout amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d3">The fluctuating interest rate influences the account value, which determines the payout upon a suicide-related death within 24 months—no additional interest is accrued, so lower rates may affect the total sum paid out.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d">
      <data key="d3">Fluctuations in the monthly interest rate may reduce the account value’s growth, increasing the risk that it becomes insufficient to meet ongoing monthly deductions, triggering a notification.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">A changing interest rate impacts the accumulation of account value, influencing whether monthly deductions can be met; if not, the policy enters a 61-day grace period before lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">A fluctuating interest rate may affect the account value, influencing whether any residual value remains after a policy lapse triggered by missed payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">Changes in the monthly interest rate affect the accumulation of account value, which in turn determines how much is available for payout upon policy lapse after subtracting surrender charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4227c22a-2b59-4bc0-8179-61e11d7945c0" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines timing</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a1217f3-3b27-4703-ab9b-bb1e1e9a2eff" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">floor rate</data>
    </edge>
