    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9">
      <data key="d3">Interest rates vary by policy year, impacting the growth of the account balance, which in turn affects the magnitude of monthly deductions based on the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">Credited interest rates can change per policy year, affecting how much interest accrues and thus influencing the total loan interest subject to monthly deduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="267656a2-1874-42ab-acb1-f06594a6ea4e">
      <data key="d3">The variation in credited interest rates across policy years affects the amount of daily interest added to the account value during those periods.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">Since the credited interest rate varies by policy year, it determines the basis for calculating daily interest credits throughout that year. Without such yearly-specific rates, accurate daily calculations would not be possible.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">Variations in credited interest rates per policy year depend on underlying financial conditions, but they cannot fall below the 2.0% guaranteed minimum.</data>
      <data key="d4">bound by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">Variations in credited interest rates across policy years encompass the current rate of 3.5%, meaning today’s rate is consistent with potential future adjustments based on policy conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">includes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">Differing credited interest rates across policy years suggest an ongoing process where rates are adjusted periodically, possibly on a monthly basis, to reflect changing conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">explained by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">The variation in credited interest rates over time affects the accumulation of the account value, which directly influences the total death benefit under Option B. However, the statement about interest rates does not explain or depend on the formula used for calculating the increasing death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Variations in credited interest rates affect how Account Value increases, making the timing and magnitude of interest application critical to understanding the overall accumulation formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">Variable credited interest rates determine how quickly the account value increases, which indirectly affects the affordability and sustainability of ongoing cost-of-insurance charges tied to mortality risk.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The possibility of variable interest rates affects how quickly the account value grows, influencing whether it stays above the level necessary to prevent entering the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences account value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4b6ce116-aa6c-469a-a8fe-6d1411d47285" target="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">sets maximum limit</data>
    </edge>
