    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9">
      <data key="d3">Variations in credited interest rates based on account value impact the total amount subject to monthly deductions, thereby affecting the actual deduction occurring on the Monthly Deduction Date.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The differing interest rates applied to various account sizes determine the amount of loan interest charged, which is subsequently deducted from the account value on the Monthly Deduction Date.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="267656a2-1874-42ab-acb1-f06594a6ea4e">
      <data key="d3">The existence of different credited interest rates for various account value amounts explains why interest is credited daily—it allows dynamic application of rates tailored to specific balance thresholds over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">Since different account value levels have distinct credited interest rates, the method described in fact_sentence_1—daily interest based on the current rate—is subject to variation depending on the account size.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">Credited interest rates can differ based on account value, yet remain constrained by the 2.0% guaranteed minimum, ensuring no rate falls below this threshold regardless of tiered structures.</data>
      <data key="d4">bound by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">Variations in credited interest rates according to account value imply that the standard 3.5% rate might not apply uniformly across all accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">Differing interest rates assigned to various account sizes could coexist with periodic updates to the overall rate, meaning that even if one’s account qualifies for a higher rate, it remains subject to future monthly revisions.</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to temporal change</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">Higher account values may lead to different credited interest rates, which in turn influence the growth of the account value used in calculating the increasing death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Variations in credited interest rates according to account value impact how premiums and fees translate into actual Account Value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">Credited interest rates depend on account value levels, which are affected by ongoing costs such as the cost of insurance (COI). Thus, variations in COI impact the growth trajectory of the account value, influencing eligibility for higher or lower interest credits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">Variable interest rates affecting account value depend on accumulated balances, which themselves result from premium allocations after deducting fees like the 3% charge mentioned in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Variable interest rates tied to account value levels impact how rapidly the account grows or shrinks, thereby influencing whether it dips below the threshold that triggers the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">Variations in interest rates applied to account value affect its growth, thereby influencing the cash surrender value calculation outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">The variation in interest rates based on account value affects the accumulation of funds that determine the cash surrender value upon policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">Higher account values due to variable interest crediting could increase the payout in case of suicide within two years, though the total remains capped at the account value regardless of interest variations.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences outcome</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d3">While interest is typically credited to the account value based on its size, this rule does not apply if the insured dies by suicide within two years—the account value paid out includes no accrued interest regardless of account level.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional override</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d">
      <data key="d3">Higher interest rates on larger account values can prevent insufficient balances, reducing the likelihood of receiving a notification about inadequate funds for monthly deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">Higher account values due to tiered interest rates increase the pool available for payout upon lapse, directly affecting the amount returned after surrender charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">Variations in interest rates affecting account value could influence whether the balance suffices to meet monthly deductions, thereby impacting eligibility for the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
