    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="82af251d-d19c-45d0-95c3-15db9a931c70">
      <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit (Option A) ensures the death benefit matches the specified amount, making it consistent and predictable upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e">
      <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit option provides a fixed payout equal to the specified amount, offering predictability. This contrasts with Option B, which allows an increasing death benefit based on account growth and is accessible only through a formal request.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit provides a fixed payout equal to the specified amount, serving as a baseline for coverage. Upgrading beyond this level necessitates additional verification through evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">Option A provides a fixed death benefit equal to the specified amount, whereas Option B increases the benefit by adding the account value, making it more dynamic based on investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">comparative</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit specifies how the payout is calculated if selected. This fixed-value option allows for potential changes only under defined conditions such as providing proof of insurability and paying a fee.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit is set equal to the Specified Amount, and this fixed amount is adjusted downward by any unpaid policy loans before being paid out.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="63e08fa1-6c41-4b13-8505-3af19ee3b242">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that under Option A, the death benefit matches the specified amount, providing essential context that supports why the $400,000 figure in fact_sentence_1 represents a stable, non-increasing payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="c7b13fca-a0cc-4be7-b051-d4ce5ea2b5ca">
      <data key="d3">The stated death benefit being equal to the specified amount under Option A validates the stable, unchanging nature of the $400,000 coverage tied to the $200 monthly premium.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="38c15270-6db4-451e-bef6-7610864a498c">
      <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit structure depends on regular payments meeting the minimum threshold to remain active and effective.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98" target="c427846c-ffb1-42e7-abbe-84ee0c48f7e8">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that the Level Death Benefit (Option A) equals the specified amount, thereby confirming the meaning and validity of the $400,000 figure stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
