    <edge source="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e" target="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98">
      <data key="d3">Option B offers a growing death benefit tied to the account value and requires a request to activate. It stands in contrast to Option A, where the death benefit remains constant regardless of account performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">The availability of Option B (Increasing Death Benefit) allows for a death benefit calculation based on the sum of the specified amount and account value. This feature is contingent on requesting the option.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d3">The availability of Option B (increasing death benefit) upon request exemplifies the general condition that changing death benefit options is permitted under specified terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">Requesting Option B (increasing death benefit) triggers the need for evidence of insurability due to increased risk exposure associated with higher coverage levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e" target="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda">
      <data key="d3">The availability of the Increasing Death Benefit option necessitates a formal request, which incurs a $50 processing fee as part of the change process.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The availability of the Increasing Death Benefit option influences potential payout amounts, but actual payment occurs only after reducing any outstanding loans, meaning the final benefit depends on both the chosen option and debt status.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
