    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9">
      <data key="d3">The increasing death benefit depends on the account value, which is reduced over time due to regular monthly deductions. Therefore, the deduction schedule influences the final benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">The method used to calculate the increasing death benefit depends on the account value, which is affected by monthly deductions like the administrative fee.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The Increasing Death Benefit depends on the Account Value, so reductions due to loan interest deductions affect its final payout, making the timing and magnitude of such deductions relevant.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="d8801d10-4c5d-4ab8-88e5-7f8a5417a886">
      <data key="d3">The Increasing Death Benefit increases with the Account Value, which also affects the basis for calculating the Cost of Insurance.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="267656a2-1874-42ab-acb1-f06594a6ea4e">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of account value in the increasing death benefit means that daily interest credits contribute incrementally to the overall death benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The increasing death benefit formula depends on the account value, which accumulates through daily interest crediting based on the current rate, making the interest rate a key driver of the benefit’s growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">drives</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">The increasing death benefit formula includes the account value, which accumulates through credited interest. Therefore, the existence of a guaranteed minimum interest rate helps sustain the account’s growth that feeds into this benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">The inclusion of the account value in the Increasing Death Benefit depends on its accumulated value, which is determined by factors such as the applied interest rate of 3.5%.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">The increasing death benefit formula includes the account value, which grows based on the crediting interest rate. Therefore, changes in the interest rate indirectly impact the magnitude of the account value component in the death benefit calculation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="014c1341-ae5d-4598-84e5-2e2c6369bc50">
      <data key="d3">The definition of the increasing death benefit includes the account value, meaning that fluctuations in the account value due to variable interest rates could impact the final payout. Yet, the existence of differing annual interest rates is independent of the structural rule defining Option B’s benefit computation.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The increasing death benefit relies on the account value, which is affected by the credited interest rate that varies depending on account size.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="82af251d-d19c-45d0-95c3-15db9a931c70">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the formula for the Increasing Death Benefit (Specified Amount + Account Value), which contrasts with the fixed nature of the currently selected Level Death Benefit described in Fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98">
      <data key="d3">Option B enhances the death benefit beyond the specified amount by incorporating the account value, unlike Option A, which maintains a static payout regardless of account growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">comparative</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e">
      <data key="d3">The rule defining the death benefit under Option B depends on the prior decision to select this option, which requires an explicit request.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">The calculation method for the increasing death benefit depends on having sufficient coverage, which triggers the requirement for evidence of insurability if the policyholder seeks to upgrade.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d3">The Increasing Death Benefit option specifies how the payout is determined based on the specified amount and account value. This definition supports the conditionality described in the second sentence regarding modifying the death benefit type.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda">
      <data key="d3">The calculation method for the Increasing Death Benefit depends on the specified amount and account value, but altering this option requires paying a $50 fee.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The Increasing Death Benefit is computed as the sum of the specified amount and the account value. This total is reduced by any unpaid policy loans before being paid out.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="067b4e81-7e90-4bd7-b365-5ab85f4e11f9" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
