    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="93b1df2c-da53-443f-a3aa-7213f007399b">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">benefit</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="82af251d-d19c-45d0-95c3-15db9a931c70">
      <data key="d3">While it is permissible to switch death benefit options under defined terms, the current choice remains Level Death Benefit until such a change is formally initiated.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables change</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98">
      <data key="d3">Changes to the death benefit type are possible but require meeting criteria like evidence of insurability and a $50 fee. One available option is the level death benefit, which pays out a specified fixed amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables option</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e">
      <data key="d3">Since changing death benefit options requires meeting certain conditions, the fact that Option B is available upon request aligns with those constraints.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">Since changing death benefit options requires proof of insurability and a fee, it implies that the rules governing benefits like those in Option B may only apply if the selected option remains unchanged.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires meeting specific criteria, one of which is providing evidence of insurability when selecting a higher coverage level.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional requirement</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda">
      <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options triggers a mandatory $50 processing fee, making the fee a direct consequence of the action.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The ability to change death benefit options sets up potential scenarios where beneficiaries receive adjusted payouts, which may include deductions for existing loans. This contextualizes why loan balances matter upon claim settlement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Changes to death benefit options depend on factors like insurability and fees, but also rely on sufficient account value to sustain increased costs, especially under the increasing death benefit option linked to accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">Changes to the death benefit option influence the cost of insurance, meaning the monthly COI charge may increase or decrease depending on whether the new option involves higher or lower risk exposure.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b102ef8d-368e-4580-ab94-919ed2902ef9" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">affects timing of implementation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23fed02e-7b63-40a3-a187-075ca1f36cc2" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts cost associated with changed death benefit</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3dfcb08a-0adf-411f-88ab-19e8ea63f799" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to total policy expenses affecting feasibility</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="991907c7-c569-4f3f-8dca-181add9a41c8" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
