    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="d0b12229-2191-4e81-b81d-1f73e28efe9b">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">benefit</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="d8801d10-4c5d-4ab8-88e5-7f8a5417a886">
      <data key="d3">Changing to a higher coverage level triggers the need for evidence of insurability, which may affect future COI calculations due to an updated specified amount, although the COI formula itself remains unchanged.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="82af251d-d19c-45d0-95c3-15db9a931c70">
      <data key="d3">Since evidence of insurability is necessary for increasing coverage, it applies directly to scenarios where one might consider moving away from the currently selected Level Death Benefit option.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to upgrade</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98">
      <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability ensures risk assessment before increasing coverage above the base Level Death Benefit, maintaining actuarial fairness.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability arises specifically when seeking to upgrade to a higher coverage option like Option B, making it a necessary step before activation.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability ensures that any increase in death benefit—such as transitioning into Option B—is properly validated before implementation.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d3">The need for evidence of insurability arises specifically when modifying death benefit options to increase coverage, supporting the process described in the broader rule about change eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables change</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda">
      <data key="d3">When upgrading to a higher death benefit option, proof of insurability is required, which necessitates paying a $50 processing fee as part of the change procedure.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional requirement</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Changes in coverage level necessitate proof of insurability, which may influence future account value accumulation due to shifts in premium structures and associated charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">Higher levels of coverage trigger updated COI calculations, necessitating verification of insurability due to elevated risk exposure.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28">
      <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability ensures underwriting compliance before increasing coverage, and the $50 fee covers administrative costs associated with such changes, making them jointly necessary steps.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that evidence of insurability is required for higher coverage, which aligns with fact_sentence_2 specifying such proof is necessary when switching to an increasing death benefit option—a form of enhanced coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">Increasing coverage requires evidence of insurability, which ensures risk assessment before raising the death benefit; however, any outstanding loans already reduce the final payout dollar-for-dollar, limiting net gain even after approval.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is required before increasing coverage, which affects the policy’s financial structure and may influence future surrender calculations involving account value and loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is required for increased coverage, ensuring underwriting standards are met before raising protection levels. This requirement indirectly supports policy sustainability, which also governs permissible partial withdrawals to maintain active status.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7ec6cd8c-d72d-4eb5-b2f6-b81209e1411f" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">requires evidence of insurability for activation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c52fc0f9-1225-4a1b-8f8d-4369b0a61e88" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is required for</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="5947f8b0-03de-4a78-9dc0-22b22b03ed36">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
