    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="82af251d-d19c-45d0-95c3-15db9a931c70">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a $50 fee for changing death benefit options implies that switching from the currently selected Level Death Benefit may involve financial costs, thus affecting decisions regarding plan modifications.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e">
      <data key="d3">A $50 fee is applied whenever a death benefit option is changed, such as selecting the Increasing Death Benefit, making the fee contingent on opting into this feature.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">Changing to an Increasing Death Benefit triggers a $50 fee, which impacts the financial terms associated with the benefit’s formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d3">The requirement of a $50 fee serves as a condition that accompanies any attempt to change death benefit options, influencing whether the change proceeds.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">The $50 processing fee applies specifically during upgrades to higher death benefit levels, where evidence of insurability is also mandated.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers fee</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Changes to death benefit options incur a $50 fee, which reduces the account value as described in fact_sentence_1, thereby affecting its long-term growth potential.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts account value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states a $50 fee is charged for changing death benefit options, which is reiterated and confirmed in fact_sentence_2 with identical wording and meaning.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d3">The $50 fee mentioned in fact_sentence_1 applies specifically when changing death benefit options, particularly when increasing coverage, which aligns with fact_sentence_2’s condition that such upgrades require evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options incurs a $50 fee, and any existing policy loans already reduce the death benefit, meaning upgrades may come at additional cost while also being offset by prior borrowing.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
