    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="b0f4f00a-0e54-49ad-bb1a-e78c2dfaa0d9">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loan balances are subtracted from death benefits, meaning that previous deductions such as those on the Monthly Deduction Date contribute to reducing the total available funds before payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to deduct outstanding loan balances before paying out death benefits necessitates ongoing tracking of accrued loan interest, making its regular deduction from the account value essential for accurate claims processing.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="267656a2-1874-42ab-acb1-f06594a6ea4e">
      <data key="d3">The deduction of outstanding loans from death benefit payments depends on the account value, which grows due to daily interest credits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="82af251d-d19c-45d0-95c3-15db9a931c70">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loan balances are subtracted from death benefit payments, which affects the final payout under the Level Death Benefit option currently in effect.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="11b71933-ace2-4b35-93af-02c6950eff98">
      <data key="d3">Any outstanding policy loan balance reduces the final death benefit payment, regardless of whether the benefit was originally defined as a fixed amount under Option A.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="c9f5669c-6177-45c9-9261-f97eb29d1c5e">
      <data key="d3">Since death benefit payments are reduced by outstanding loans, choosing the Increasing Death Benefit option could result in lower net payouts if significant loan balances remain unpaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="fcc5d4f1-98b6-4db9-90f4-acbeec66da4c">
      <data key="d3">Any outstanding policy loan balance reduces the death benefit payout, meaning that even if the death benefit is based on the specified amount plus account value, the actual payment received is lower due to debt owed.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="8062e15c-8d4b-4306-89c1-b273d1eddd40">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loan balances affect final death benefit payouts, reinforcing that such adjustments require careful consideration before modifying benefit options, especially since upgrades involve additional requirements like medical proof.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects payout</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The deduction of outstanding loans from death benefits depends on the level of Account Value, which itself is determined by premiums, fees, and interest—directly tied to the definition provided in the first fact.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="5d474352-9ca8-4438-912d-d598a9dfc72e">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit, meaning lower available funds may result from high cumulative costs like COI, making it harder to maintain sufficient account value to cover debts without depleting the estate.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit, meaning less money remains from the accumulated Account Value derived from premiums after fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce death benefit payouts, so if a policy lapses due to low account value—even during a grace period—the remaining balance owed could diminish what beneficiaries receive.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability when increasing death benefits relates to the risk management aspect behind loan adjustments that affect payout amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that death benefits are adjusted downward by unpaid policy loans, which aligns precisely with fact_sentence_2 stating that such loans reduce the death benefit equally in dollar terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28">
      <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options incurs a $50 fee, which adds to the overall cost of adjusting coverage; this change also influences how much remains after deducting outstanding loans from the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable policy loan (90% of account value) determines the upper bound of what can be subtracted from the death benefit payment, directly influencing the net payout described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit reductions due to unpaid loans indirectly influence available account value, thereby affecting the maximum allowable partial withdrawal under policy rules.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is diminished by outstanding loans, just as the cash surrender value is reduced by them, showing shared dependency on loan balances across different payout scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit calculations are affected by outstanding loans, similar to how cash surrender value is diminished by them. Both mechanisms reflect loan liabilities reducing final payouts under different scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit calculations consider outstanding loans, similar to how surrender value deducts them; thus, loan balances affect payout amounts under both scenarios, though one occurs upon death and the other on voluntary termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20">
      <data key="d3">If there was material misrepresentation within two years of issuance, the insurer may deny the death benefit entirely, making the deduction of loan balances irrelevant.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that death benefits are reduced by unpaid loans, whereas fact_sentence_2 specifies that in cases of suicide within two years, only the account value is paid—even if there are outstanding loans. This means loan deductions would still apply unless explicitly waived under the suicide clause.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional limitation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines standard deduction of loans from death benefits, while fact_sentence_2 specifies an exceptional case where no interest accrues on the account value if suicide occurs within two years, further reducing potential payout beyond just loan offsets.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional dependence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d">
      <data key="d3">A low account value due to unpaid deductions could impair repayment of policy loans, thereby reducing the final death benefit. This creates an indirect dependency on maintaining sufficient funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">If the account value falls short of covering monthly costs, the policy enters a 61-day grace period before lapsing, preserving the potential for future death benefit payouts—even if loans remain outstanding.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, any remaining account value after surrender charges is returned, but outstanding loans still reduce the net payout, aligning with the rule that loans are subtracted before final disbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">A policy lapse due to missed premiums prevents future death benefit payments, rendering the rule about deducting loans irrelevant since no claim occurs. However, the presence of outstanding loans affects what remains upon surrender before lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="423d4dc7-0297-40e7-bb6c-63599ccfd193" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">reduce death benefit</data>
    </edge>
