      <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires fulfilling a procedural obligation involving a $50 fee, establishing a direct consequence linked to the initial action.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5ce89780-40fe-4552-b6df-64321fe6f11d" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options allows adjustments to the policy terms, including those affecting how future payments are calculated. This includes reductions from outstanding loans, which diminish the net amount payable upon death.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5ce89780-40fe-4552-b6df-64321fe6f11d" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options affects how much coverage is maintained, potentially influencing whether the account value remains above the threshold needed to sustain the original death benefit. If adjustments result in lower funding levels, the death benefit may be reduced accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
