      <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability applies specifically when modifying death benefits to increase coverage, thus qualifying the broader action of changing death benefit options.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains condition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd" target="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28">
      <data key="d3">Increasing the death benefit necessitates proof of insurability, and this change triggers a mandatory $50 processing fee.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional fee</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Changes in death benefit options depend on insurability and may impact account value calculations, particularly if additional premiums are required to maintain new coverage tiers.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">Requirements to provide evidence of insurability when increasing death benefits depend on current policy value, which is influenced by how premiums are allocated after expenses.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that modifying death benefits to increase coverage demands evidence of insurability, supporting and exemplifying the broader requirement stated in fact_sentence_1 about needing such documentation when elevating coverage levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd" target="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that increasing death benefit coverage necessitates proof of insurability, which justifies the $50 processing fee described in fact_sentence_1 as part of the change procedure.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Increasing the death benefit impacts the net payout by introducing potential loan liabilities, meaning the final payment reflects deductions such as unpaid loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de1c1a89-7d0d-4ac2-a0d1-29a4297f625d" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">requires evidence of insurability when increased</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="97bd9e72-b7b7-4d32-bb9f-9d841b5363c6" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">influences need for evidence of insurability</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df2d24d3-0bb2-41ab-9623-5ca83c0983e3" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">affects eligibility for coverage increase requiring evidence of insurability</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3080a58-5b87-49ba-89b9-3985bf06a69b" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts determination of insurability requirements</data>
