    <edge source="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28" target="712d5685-87e1-43db-ad4c-f07ca2f1a8cd">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28" target="b4570006-35bc-45b4-9207-28ad0fa1179d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28" target="5ce89780-40fe-4552-b6df-64321fe6f11d">
      <data key="d3">The necessity of paying a $50 fee arises specifically because the policy allows modifications to death benefit options, making the fee contingent upon the prior permission to alter them.</data>
      <data key="d4">modified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28" target="845cc8e6-40ef-4fe2-9955-b02c0bf1b0cd">
      <data key="d3">The $50 fee applies specifically to changes in death benefit options, including cases where increased coverage requires evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">incurred by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">The $50 fee enforces financial accountability for altering death benefits, reinforcing the need for evidence of insurability to mitigate insurer risk during upgrades.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28" target="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reiterates the $50 processing fee for changing death benefit options, matching precisely with fact_sentence_1 and supported by shared contextual information in both summaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to pay a $50 fee when switching death benefit types supports the mechanism described in fact_sentence_1, where adjusted death benefits may result in lower payouts due to existing loan balances.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b21cd7be-f875-478b-88df-a908f06117be" target="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has associated processing fee</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10b4c258-f5af-47b2-a856-df2890b9f429" target="e997d92e-ef77-4280-a56b-679e43d39e28">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is the processing fee for changing death benefit option</data>
    </edge>
