    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="ef169c65-7425-4e6e-8a07-c198c96e70f8">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="660375a7-948b-4b52-b8da-573b6256626d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="5ce89780-40fe-4552-b6df-64321fe6f11d">
      <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit after subtracting outstanding loans reflects an outcome influenced by prior decisions about borrowing against the policy, such as whether to increase or adjust the death benefit through available options.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal is constrained by the need to preserve enough account value to sustain the policy's validity, which indirectly influences the net death benefit available after subtracting outstanding loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">The maximum policy loan amount—capped at 90% of the account value—directly determines the largest possible reduction to the death benefit upon payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit; the interest rate on these loans, set relative to a market index, determines how quickly the loan balance grows and thus impacts the net payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit after subtracting outstanding loans depends on the accumulated debt, including interest accrued at rates such as the minimum 4%. This interest contributes to the total loan balance reducing the payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">A drop in account value below the required minimum can trigger a reduction in the death benefit, even if no loans exist. This reflects a structural safeguard ensuring policy integrity under financial stress.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">The reduction in death benefit due to outstanding loans is exacerbated over time if interest accumulates on those loans, increasing the total debt owed.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4">
      <data key="d3">The amount of outstanding policy loans impacts the death benefit payment, and since loan interest adjusts annually, it influences the growing balance of those loans over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit. Fact_sentence_2 specifies that this reduction occurs on a dollar-for-dollar basis, providing clarity on the mechanism.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit deduction due to unpaid loans depends on accumulated loan balance, which includes accrued interest. Annual interest payments help maintain accurate tracking of the growing liability.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, setting context for how liabilities affect payouts. This principle extends into fact_sentence_2, where similar loan deductions appear alongside surrender charges to determine cash surrender value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cbd1c2ae-0b6e-4d70-b72d-0bd4e47b3e1e" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">reduced by outstanding policy loans</data>
    </edge>
