    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="c19e85c6-c1d2-4678-8312-3597644a0fb6">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are permitted at any time, but they cannot be less than $500, ensuring a threshold level of financial significance for each transaction.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">Making partial withdrawals at any time results in a decrease in the account value, as funds are taken out of the policy's accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="24c5ad15-0f69-45ce-be24-f83388bd917d">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are allowed at any time, but beginning in year 11, they become exempt from withdrawal charges, making long-term access more financially favorable.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional exemption</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are allowed at any time, but the maximum allowable amount is constrained by the need to maintain the policy's active status, ensuring sufficient funds remain in the account.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals can reduce the account value over time, potentially causing it to drop below the minimum required level, which triggers a decrease in the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are allowed at any time, but if conducted during the first decade, each withdrawal incurs a $25 fee, limiting their frequency or desirability early in the policy term.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional cost</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals allow access to funds at any time, reflecting flexibility in using the account value. This contrasts with policy loans, which permit borrowing up to 90% of the same account value, offering an alternative method of accessing funds without withdrawing outright.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals rely on the defined method of Account Value accumulation, ensuring that such actions are feasible only within the framework established by premium contributions, fees, and interest crediting.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals depend on having an existing Account Value built from premiums after deducting the 3% expense charge; thus, the availability of withdrawals hinges on the funding mechanism outlined in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are permissible regardless of the policy's financial status, meaning they can occur even after the Account Value has fallen into the grace period window defined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">independently permitted</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals affect the account value over time, influencing whether a future surrender would result in lower net payouts due to accumulated surrender charges still applying before year 15.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="532a373e-e61f-4b69-8c7f-20c934ef1490" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has partial withdrawal access</data>
    </edge>
