      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">year range</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="da874c5a-3c4d-4aa0-b32f-87b05f43145b">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">year range</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="c0db09ff-4e2d-4060-994e-6431defda972">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">percentage</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="0fc7585d-26fe-445d-972b-098e1ca9a032">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="39d79633-feb2-4bf2-8743-bcfc38773c16">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="1bae4c5d-90f8-4402-b980-d186ec5da414">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d3">A minimum withdrawal of $500 applies to all partial withdrawals made from the account value, limiting how small such transactions can be.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the minimum threshold for withdrawals, ensuring transactions have meaningful impact. This constraint works in tandem with fact_sentence_2, which determines the maximum possible withdrawal without jeopardizing policy validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">A minimum withdrawal amount of $500 ensures that only meaningful transactions occur, enabling partial withdrawals that subsequently lower the Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="24c5ad15-0f69-45ce-be24-f83388bd917d">
      <data key="d3">The $500 minimum ensures withdrawals meet a basic threshold, while the absence of charges from year 11 onward incentivizes delayed access to funds without penalty.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the minimum allowable withdrawal amount, ensuring any transaction qualifies for processing. This condition enables the application of the annual fee described in fact_sentence_2, which targets withdrawals occurring within the first ten years.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">A minimum withdrawal of $500 ensures that large enough reductions do not destabilize the account balance, thereby helping prevent the account from falling below the required threshold that would trigger a death benefit reduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents reduction</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The requirement of a $500 minimum partial withdrawal (fact_sentence_2) depends on the existence of an Account Value, which is detailed in fact_sentence_1 as being built from premiums, adjusted for fees and interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables access</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The $500 minimum partial withdrawal rule depends on having accumulated Account Value, which results from premiums being allocated post-expense charge—making the timing and adequacy of premium deposits relevant to whether withdrawals meet the threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that partial withdrawals be at least $500 means such actions can significantly impact the Account Value, possibly causing it to fall below the level needed to sustain monthly charges and thus initiate the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f2ec755f-1895-4201-a41a-28793e47a40d" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has minimum withdrawal amount</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1bae4c5d-90f8-4402-b980-d186ec5da414" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines minimum partial withdrawal</data>
    </edge>
