      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">year range</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="8af78044-62d7-40f8-a6af-0acb70a80b8a">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">percentage</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="fbb81e3e-03e1-434a-969a-9c5f80fd92b3">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="6fd349cc-2aa7-408b-8dd7-64703ca0b292">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="89082a19-dc58-4a1c-bf56-60fb9c6e482b">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is reduced by outstanding loans, meaning that higher loan balances may restrict the usable portion of the account value available for partial withdrawals without jeopardizing policy status.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d3">The ability to withdraw funds anytime is subject to limits; specifically, the withdrawal cannot exceed what remains after reserving enough to sustain the policy’s validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the upper boundary of withdrawals based on preserving policy status, which complements fact_sentence_1's lower limit of $500 to fully define permissible withdrawal ranges.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal depends on maintaining sufficient account value to sustain the policy's validity, meaning any withdrawal reduces the available balance accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals cannot exceed what is necessary to maintain the policy’s active status; if they do, the account value could fall below the threshold that sustains the death benefit, potentially triggering its reduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the cap on how much can be withdrawn without invalidating the policy, ensuring that sufficient funds remain to maintain it. Fact_sentence_2 adds a financial cost to each withdrawal event within the early policy years, applying regardless of the withdrawal size.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="24c5ad15-0f69-45ce-be24-f83388bd917d">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the cap on partial withdrawals based on policy sustainability, ensuring sufficient funds remain to maintain the policy. Fact_sentence_2 indicates that once past year 10, withdrawal costs are waived, offering financial relief for late-stage withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 defines the upper limit for partial withdrawals based on preserving policy status using account value. Fact sentence 2 specifies that policy loans are capped at 90% of the same account value metric.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The rule limiting partial withdrawals to the excess of Account Value over maintenance requirements relies on an accurate understanding of how Account Value is accumulated, as defined here.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The restriction on partial withdrawals ensures that sufficient Account Value remains to sustain the policy, thereby affecting how much of each premium contribution ultimately contributes to usable reserves.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Withdrawing more than the safe limit risks reducing the Account Value so much that it triggers the 61-day grace period mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are restricted not only by minimum amounts and timing but also by the requirement to preserve enough account value to avoid triggering surrender charges, making the existence of such charges a key factor in determining allowable withdrawal levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are constrained by the need to retain sufficient account value to keep the policy in force, reinforcing the importance of financial stability. This constraint complements the rule that increasing coverage requires proof of insurability to ensure long-term viability.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Limitations on partial withdrawals ensure sufficient account value remains to cover potential future loan repayments, which in turn impact final death benefit calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="087940c1-1c93-482a-aecb-90cebb3f6525" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">used to determine minimum retained amount for policy in force</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fbb81e3e-03e1-434a-969a-9c5f80fd92b3" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
