    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d3">The presence of a $25 annual charge for withdrawals during years 1–10 modifies how frequently the ability to withdraw funds can be exercised, effectively constraining the freedom mentioned in the earlier statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies a recurring $25 fee applied to withdrawals made in early policy years, reinforcing the importance of meeting the $500 minimum outlined in fact_sentence_1 to justify such transactions financially.</data>
      <data key="d4">incurred by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a recurring fee for any partial withdrawal taken in the first ten years, affecting the net gain from such actions. This constraint operates under the condition established by fact_sentence_1—that withdrawals are permissible only up to a certain threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="24c5ad15-0f69-45ce-be24-f83388bd917d">
      <data key="d3">Withdrawal fees apply only within the first ten years; beyond that period, no charge is assessed regardless of withdrawal amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">exempt by time</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">Making a partial withdrawal reduces the account value, as funds are taken out of the policy’s accumulated balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Withdrawal fees during the first decade directly impact the Account Value calculation described in fact_sentence_1, reducing the net gain from premiums due to additional costs incurred.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts account value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">Withdrawal fees during years 1–10 reflect restrictions on accessing funds that were initially deposited via premiums, which themselves undergo a 3% expense charge before being credited to the Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period exists to allow time to restore sufficient Account Value after it declines—potentially due to fees like those incurred from early withdrawals described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 specifies a fixed $25 fee for withdrawals in years 1–10, it indirectly supports the rationale behind fact_sentence_1's higher percentage-based surrender charge by illustrating multiple layers of costs associated with early fund access.</data>
      <data key="d4">supprts rationale</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c18bf990-2b3e-45b1-949f-7004457b8ad0" target="41c5d4e5-1a4c-49c6-93b9-86a0c912c977">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is the charge per withdrawal</data>
    </edge>
