    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="5ce89780-40fe-4552-b6df-64321fe6f11d">
      <data key="d3">A drop in account value below the required minimum triggers an automatic reduction in the death benefit, meaning any prior decisions about adjusting the death benefit option become constrained by current financial performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers reduction of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans directly diminish the available death benefit; if such loans cause the account value to fall too low, the death benefit may also be adjusted downward.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d3">A decline in account value due to withdrawals risks falling below the minimum threshold, thereby necessitating adjustments to the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="c7dd6118-69b1-47ff-a5b4-fc2086782f63">
      <data key="d3">If the account value drops below the necessary level due to excessive or frequent withdrawals—such as those under $500—the death benefit may be adjusted downward, emphasizing why minimum withdrawal rules exist.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers limitation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">A drop in account value below the required minimum risks reducing the death benefit, which limits how much can be withdrawn without jeopardizing policy validity, thus constraining partial withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">A decline in Account Value due to withdrawals risks triggering a reduction in the death benefit if it falls beneath the required minimum level.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">A reduction in the account value below a threshold impacts the death benefit, which influences how much can be borrowed via a policy loan since the loan cap is tied to that same account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">A low account value may trigger a reduction in the death benefit, compounding the effect of pre-existing policy loans, which already decrease the benefit dollar-for-dollar.</data>
      <data key="d4">compounds with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">A decrease in account value due to factors like loan accumulation could threaten meeting minimum thresholds, potentially reducing the death benefit. Interest accruing on policy loans contributes to growing debt, further eroding account value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">A decrease in account value below the minimum threshold reduces the death benefit, which influences the overall financial outcome upon surrender. This ties into the formula for Cash Surrender Value, where lower account value leads to a smaller base amount after deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="06652a40-48d6-4ba6-941f-b41252fa67d2" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">may be reduced if account value falls below minimum</data>
    </edge>
