      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="8cd92610-aa20-42b0-b212-e9c1ff20ad1d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="b752d1b6-c494-498b-9a33-c25e19acd540">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is diminished by outstanding loans, the cap on loans at 90% of account value limits the extent to which the death benefit can be reduced.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="0ca94573-8672-4372-9074-da09fea51f72">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans provide a means to borrow against the account value, capped at 90%, serving as a funding mechanism separate from direct withdrawals. These loans differ from partial withdrawals, which involve actual disbursement of funds from the account balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="78ae0a1e-3056-4039-bbc1-344b5b6b24a5">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that policy loans may not exceed 90% of the account value. This threshold indirectly influences the available funds for other transactions like partial withdrawals, though it does not constrain them directly.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">Since the maximum policy loan is determined by the Account Value, any decrease in Account Value—such as through partial withdrawals—affects the borrowing capacity accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable policy loan—set at 90% of the account value—is contingent upon the account value remaining above the minimum required level to maintain full death benefit coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the account value, and any such loan incurs interest calculated as Moody's Corporate Bond Index plus 1.5%, linking the loan’s affordability to market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan amount is set at 90% of the account value, enabling borrowers to access substantial funds while leaving room for future growth. Interest on these loans may accumulate and increase the total repayment burden over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable policy loan is capped at 90% of the account value, setting the potential scale of debt against the policy's equity. This level of borrowing directly reduces the death benefit, meaning larger loans result in proportionally greater reductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan amount sets a limit on funds drawn from the policy, which directly impacts the calculation of the Cash Surrender Value by reducing it through outstanding loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The policy loan cap of 90% of Account Value, stated in fact_sentence_2, depends entirely on the method of Account Value accumulation detailed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The ability to take a loan up to 90% of the Account Value relies on the Account Value being built from premiums after deducting the 3% expense charge, making the funding mechanism foundational to loan eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans up to 90% of Account Value provide a mechanism to prevent lapse during the 61-day grace period caused by insufficient funds to meet monthly charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans up to 90% of account value may deplete reserves needed to avoid triggering surrender charges if the policy is later canceled before year 15.</data>
      <data key="d4">independently relevant</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">The rule that death benefits are reduced by outstanding loans depends on the existence of those loans, whose limit (up to 90% of account value) sets the potential scale of reduction mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4c263d73-cbef-4497-b5e1-5bd4f1016b44" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines maximum policy loan</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b91be823-d540-4389-8b16-1a2754286a45" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines maximum policy loan</data>
    </edge>
