    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="ae677cb8-c3d3-4946-8917-09bf5e91bc3c">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="ea19fdba-e572-4fcc-8da4-f4c2f4e41b4d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="aee8b273-9ac8-4c09-9eed-613fc814f708">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">A variable interest rate linked to a bond index governs the growth of policy loan balances, which in turn reduces the total death benefit available upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">A loan can be taken up to 90% of the account value, with its cost influenced by a variable interest rate set at Moody's Corporate Bond Index plus 1.5%, affecting overall repayment burden.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4">
      <data key="d3">The variable interest rate for policy loans, set as Moody's Corporate Bond Index plus 1.5%, is applied consistently each year and adjusted annually on January 1 to reflect current market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d3">The loan interest rate is determined by adding 1.5% to Moody's Corporate Bond Index, but it is subject to a minimum cap of 4%, preventing it from falling lower than this threshold even if the index declines significantly.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans accrue variable interest linked to a bond index, which increases the debt burden over time; this growing obligation reduces the final death benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">The variable interest rate defined in sentence 1 determines how much additional interest is applied to the loan balance over time, leading to compounding growth if not repaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">determines</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e">
      <data key="d3">The variable interest rate on policy loans, determined by adding 1.5% to Moody's Corporate Bond Index, establishes the basis for periodic payments. Interest may be paid annually, reflecting how often the accrued amount is settled.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The variable interest rate on policy loans, set relative to a bond index, increases the outstanding loan balance over time, thereby reducing the eventual cash surrender value when loans remain unpaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Loan interest rates influence the financial impact of withdrawing funds via policy loans, thereby impacting the long-term sustainability and size of the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">Loan interest rates increase borrowing costs over time, making it more expensive to delay surrender; higher accumulated interest could amplify the effective burden of surrender charges later in the term.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts surrender value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e368ca5d-9a84-44c5-8255-6a362f9180fb" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
    </edge>
