      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">year range</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="d168ebde-043a-4a23-b8c0-68ab029ce728">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">percentage</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="b63c26c0-c831-4c64-abd4-defe137d8bfe">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="3577aa83-0af9-44af-81ae-39132a5956ae">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="2d834807-ec36-4261-b409-c082a1dc2acf">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">A minimum loan interest rate of 4% increases the overall loan burden, thereby amplifying the reduction in the death benefit due to unpaid loans upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases reduction</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">A minimum interest rate of 4% ensures that despite being variable and linked to an external bond index, the loan cost remains bounded above, providing stability and protection against extremely low rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4">
      <data key="d3">The minimum loan interest rate of 4% sets a lower bound, ensuring rates never fall below this threshold even after annual adjustments on January 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">sets boundary</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e">
      <data key="d3">The minimum loan interest rate being set at 4% establishes the baseline cost of borrowing, enabling the possibility of annual interest payments on policy loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">A minimum interest rate of 4% ensures that any accrued interest applied to the loan balance has a baseline threshold, preventing arbitrarily low rates from undermining the policy's financial integrity.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">The minimum loan interest rate ensures that borrowers pay at least 4%, affecting the financial burden of taking out a loan. This interest accumulates over time without altering how the loan reduces the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The minimum loan interest rate influences the cost of borrowing against the policy, which affects the total amount deducted from the account value when calculating the cash surrender value. This makes the interest rate relevant to understanding the overall impact of loans on final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">A higher loan interest rate reduces net returns on the account value since borrowed amounts accrue interest, thereby diminishing growth potential over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8aa26aa0-64eb-4bf9-8e50-7bbe386d4b8f" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">defines</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3577aa83-0af9-44af-81ae-39132a5956ae" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to minimum interest rate</data>
    </edge>
