      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4" target="7db79d1e-b93d-4575-a99b-d2d4389d10bd">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">Annual adjustments to loan interest rates affect the total accumulated debt, which in turn reduces the net death benefit payable upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">Annual adjustment of loan interest rates on January 1 ensures that the rate—calculated as Moody's Corporate Bond Index plus 1.5%—remains aligned with prevailing economic benchmarks.</data>
      <data key="d4">drives</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d3">Annual adjustments to loan interest rates on January 1 allow the rate to fluctuate above or remain at the minimum of 4%, depending on market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">adjusts within</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4" target="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e">
      <data key="d3">The annual adjustment of loan interest rates on January 1 enables predictable scheduling of interest payments, allowing borrowers to plan for annual payment obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">Annual adjustment of loan interest rates influences the amount of interest added to the loan balance, affecting long-term debt accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">drives</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">Annual interest rate adjustments influence the growth of outstanding policy loans, which in turn reduce the death benefit proportionally. This creates an indirect link where changing interest conditions gradually increase the reduction in death benefit over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Annual adjustment of loan interest rates affects the economic burden of policy loans, which in turn impact the net Account Value after deductions for accrued interest and reduced death benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cf924772-6bbf-4e40-9230-bf1ef6eb4b8a" target="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">trigger date for annual loan rate adjustment</data>
    </edge>
