    <edge source="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">Annual interest payments on policy loans contribute to the total outstanding loan balance, which reduces the final death benefit upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">Annual payment of interest on policy loans implies regular financial obligations tied to the underlying variable rate, which is set as Moody's Corporate Bond Index plus 1.5%, ensuring alignment with market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d3">Annual interest payments on policy loans imply that interest accumulates over time, contingent upon a defined minimum rate such as 4%, ensuring the charge remains above a threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e" target="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4">
      <data key="d3">Annual interest payments depend on fixed-rate adjustments occurring each January 1, ensuring consistent terms for repayment cycles.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that interest on policy loans may be paid annually, offering a payout option. This contrasts with fact_sentence_2, which explains that instead of being paid out, interest can accumulate by being added to the loan balance, thereby increasing its size over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">The repayment or accumulation of interest on policy loans influences the total loan balance, which subsequently reduces the death benefit. This creates a cumulative effect where ongoing interest increases the offset against the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The annual payment of interest on policy loans contributes to the accumulation of debt, which reduces the available cash surrender value. This ongoing cost is accounted for when calculating the final payout upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4502bdc5-ed6a-4c27-b470-81e831c0329a" target="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has interest payment</data>
    </edge>
