      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="506ac465-0fca-4316-bec7-a8fcc5337cee">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">Accrued interest on policy loans raises the loan balance, leading to a larger deduction from the death benefit upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">Accrued interest being added to policy loan balances reduces available account value, which might cause it to fall below the minimum required level, thereby risking a reduction in the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">Accrued interest increases the overall loan balance, meaning that even if the initial loan stays within the 90% threshold, its effective cost grows due to compounding interest; thus, managing interest helps preserve the original loan limit's utility.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases cost</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">The practice of adding interest to the loan balance, as stated in sentence 2, requires a clear definition of the interest rate, such as the one specified in sentence 1, to function predictably.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d3">Accumulating interest by adding it to the loan balance means borrowers effectively owe more over time, making the presence of a defined minimum rate essential for predicting long-term cost implications.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4">
      <data key="d3">The addition of interest to the loan balance depends on the current interest rate, which is reset each year on January 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 indicates that unpaid interest accumulates by being added to the loan balance, creating compound growth. In contrast, fact_sentence_1 presents an alternate scenario where such interest is not rolled into the principal but distributed annually.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">When interest on a policy loan is not paid, it compounds and adds to the loan balance, thereby increasing the total amount owed. This larger loan balance reduces the death benefit more significantly upon payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">When interest on policy loans is not paid, it compounds and adds to the loan balance, increasing the total debt owed. This higher outstanding loan amount reduces the cash surrender value upon policy cancellation.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases debt</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb9d0c8e-ec95-44e9-9a1b-b6419b2b84d9" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
    </edge>
