    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="576f22b8-5094-43c9-801f-4cc6fdd955ae">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">minimum rate</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="e4b7697b-3718-437d-a030-eb85987714fd">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="2d75fac1-149c-43e3-8e42-64694ec64047">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">year range</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="288b5ba7-d5e3-4ecc-91e7-a5a702834edf">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">year range</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="96981528-e8ab-42ef-a509-cd2dbe41d902">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">percentage</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="e8ffc2f5-2588-4dcc-82d5-0d35ad518cb2">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="81a31c62-80bc-47a7-ae40-984978abf20e">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="55b3a7c2-883a-4db4-91fe-ec38c5aa3f4e">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="5ce89780-40fe-4552-b6df-64321fe6f11d">
      <data key="d3">The reduction of the death benefit by outstanding loans affects decisions regarding altering death benefit options, particularly if higher benefits are desired despite debt obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that each dollar of loan reduces the death benefit by exactly one dollar. This detail supports and expands upon the general claim made in fact_sentence_1 about reductions due to loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit directly; if combined with an account value drop below threshold levels, the overall death benefit could face further or more severe reductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">exacerbates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">Any outstanding policy loan diminishes the death benefit equally in dollar amount, so the extent of this reduction hinges entirely on the loan balance—which itself cannot exceed 90% of the account value as per the initial rule.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">Since outstanding loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, borrowers face a direct consequence that makes managing loan balances crucial, especially given the variable interest rates applied.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit equally in dollar amount regardless of interest rates applied. While higher interest increases repayment costs, it doesn’t change the extent to which the death benefit is reduced.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="ba3411a8-2d57-4476-b841-b56888cf26a4">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that outstanding loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar means any accumulated interest from annual rate changes directly diminishes the payout, making the repayment burden more significant over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">accumulates over time</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is reduced dollar-for-dollar by the full amount of any outstanding policy loan, including accumulated interest. Therefore, unmet interest payments amplify the impact on the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e">
      <data key="d3">Since outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, any increase in the loan due to accrued interest further diminishes the payout, making timely interest management important.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the death benefit, and since they are subtracted from the account value to determine the cash surrender value, this effect carries over into the final payout upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar and also decrease the account value; therefore, the calculation of account value depends on whether any loans remain unpaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts account value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reducing the death benefit depend on the account value built via premium allocations, making the outcome of fact_sentence_1 relevant to the scope of fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">When the account value declines due to unpaid charges during the grace period, any existing policy loans continue to reduce the death benefit proportionally, compounding financial pressure on the policyholder.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit directly, meaning any remaining cash value after repayment may still be reduced further by surrender charges if the policy is canceled early.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit and also decrease the cash surrender value, showing that loan balances impact both payout scenarios under different conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="d2bec389-f814-4532-8f19-68d9fc0c9d10">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit, compounding the impact of the 8% surrender charge in year one, thereby diminishing the total cash surrender value available to the policyholder.</data>
      <data key="d4">compounds with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="be5a6946-58ba-4487-a91b-97d9949ba78f">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit and lower the cash surrender value, so any outstanding loans increase the effective cost of surrendering the policy in year 5, where a 5% surrender charge applies.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit, which affects the total payout available at surrender, where a 2% surrender charge applies in year 10, compounding its impact on the final cash value received.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit, which directly impacts the amount paid out upon surrender, when coverage officially ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans diminish the death benefit and remain subtracted from the cash surrender value when the policy is terminated, making the reduction effect concrete upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="f6b5e972-2fde-453a-98fa-9ea8711ed5fa">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans diminish the death benefit and remain subtracted even at surrender, so carrying them into year 15+ means higher net payouts due to zero surrender charges. This combination allows borrowers to maximize returns post-year 15.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit, compounding the reduction caused by suicide clauses, which limit payouts to account value. Together, these provisions may significantly lower the actual benefit paid upon death.</data>
      <data key="d4">compounds with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans diminish the death benefit and can contribute to low account value, potentially triggering the 61-day grace period when payments are not met.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit, so if a policy lapses, the outstanding loan balance reduces the amount of account value that can be recovered, potentially limiting the return to the policyholder.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces payout</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="fed25863-324a-4e70-9aea-8082dbd86103">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit directly, so even if an insured successfully obtains higher coverage through evidence of insurability, the actual payout remains reduced by prior debt obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="fc8c547c-a3db-4bf9-b939-d59fcb27dfda">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, so even though a $50 fee applies to change benefit options, the net effect depends on accumulated loan balances reducing potential payouts.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies the mechanism behind fact_sentence_1 by specifying that every dollar of loan balance reduces the death benefit by exactly one dollar, providing detail on how the subtraction occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains mechanism</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="dc50b116-f13f-40b7-a1dd-acbe416f2e14" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">reduced by outstanding policy loans</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="81a31c62-80bc-47a7-ae40-984978abf20e" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
