    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="b2fb7e0c-eab0-476d-a9e3-005cfceb82ed">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="8b64f169-6b8f-497f-9d45-45c254f0076f">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="57fdfa10-0b76-4282-a362-7bce2a4ec29f">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines cash surrender value using outstanding loans as a subtractive factor, reinforcing the idea introduced in fact_sentence_1 that loans diminish available funds. It applies the same deductive rule to a different settlement scenario—policy surrender rather than death claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">extends</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="50663f78-143a-4016-b611-650692d96c08">
      <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value depends on the current Account Value; therefore, any reduction in Account Value—such as through partial withdrawals—affects the ultimate surrender amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="14cbd8d0-a65c-4695-bdf2-4321ad3892d2">
      <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value depends on subtracting loans and surrender charges from the account value; if the account value drops too low due to such factors, it could trigger a reduction in the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="6af7d75d-09de-48d0-a36c-4995b7e25cb6">
      <data key="d3">The formula for Cash Surrender Value includes deductions for outstanding loans, meaning the extent of those loans—which are capped at 90% of Account Value—is essential to determining the net surrender outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="63a11648-dce1-4eab-baac-b85dc94452ef">
      <data key="d3">The formula for calculating cash surrender value includes outstanding loans; therefore, any increase in loan interest due to the indexed rate reduces the net payout upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="c2e2155b-e87f-4d17-86da-eb5c1aff1318">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on outstanding loans, meaning any borrowed amounts reduce the available payout; however, the actual interest charged on those loans—which includes a minimum rate—is part of what determines the accumulated debt impacting the surrender outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="02ecca85-e952-4d49-9f51-b12f5c30ef39">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on deducting outstanding loans from the account value; therefore, any accumulated interest that increases those loans further diminishes the available payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduced by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="19e2df30-bca6-4c17-a14c-779571d3b27e">
      <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding loans, including accrued interest, diminishes the cash surrender value, meaning that policies where interest accumulates over time result in lower payouts unless repaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
