    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="d2bec389-f814-4532-8f19-68d9fc0c9d10">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the general formula for determining cash surrender value, including surrender charges. Fact_sentence_2 gives a concrete example by specifying the surrender charge rate in year one, which contributes to computing the total deduction from the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the general calculation method for cash surrender value, including surrender charges. Fact_sentence_2 gives a specific example of that charge being 2% of the specified amount in year 10.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="f6b5e972-2fde-453a-98fa-9ea8711ed5fa">
      <data key="d3">The formula for Cash Surrender Value includes surrender charges, which are explicitly reduced to zero in year 15 or later, making the charge non-applicable under those conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">Knowing how the cash surrender value is calculated enables determination of the payout upon policy surrender, directly leading to the conclusion that the policy terminates at that point.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="be5a6946-58ba-4487-a91b-97d9949ba78f">
      <data key="d3">The formula for Cash Surrender Value includes subtracting surrender charges, and fact_sentence_2 specifies the rate of such a charge in year 5, providing concrete context for one component of the equation.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value is computed by subtracting surrender charges and loans from the account value. When the policyholder surrenders the policy based on this value, the coverage ceases permanently.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Cash Surrender Value includes the Account Value, which determines the amount paid upon suicide within two years. This establishes that the Account Value is central to determining payouts under specific circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value is calculated based on account value, surrender charges, and loans, forming the basis for potential payouts. In cases of suicide within two years, the account value is paid without accrued interest, modifying the effective payout despite the standard formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">The formula for Cash Surrender Value establishes the basis for calculating the amount returned upon policy lapse. When a policy lapses, any remaining account value above surrender charges is automatically paid out based on this definition.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes how cash surrender value is calculated using account value, surrender charges, and loans. Fact_sentence_2 explains that even when account value is low, the policy stays active for up to 61 days before lapsing, providing temporary protection despite inadequate funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">The definition provided in fact_sentence_2 mirrors exactly that of fact_sentence_1, confirming uniformity in expression and meaning despite being presented in separate chunks with slightly varied surrounding context.</data>
      <data key="d4">identical to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="733fa6c6-1173-4248-94bb-47741de40661">
      <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes the surrender charge, so knowing its percentage (8%) allows precise determination of the actual return when surrendering the policy in year one.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">The reduction of the death benefit due to outstanding loans aligns with the calculation of cash surrender value, where those same loans are subtracted from the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value formula includes the Account Value, which is reduced monthly by the Cost of Insurance charge described in fact_sentence_1, meaning long-term deductions diminish the value available for surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on the account value, which is reduced by the monthly $8.00 administrative fee, making the fee an indirect factor in determining the final surrender payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">Cash Surrender Value depends on the Account Value after deducting outstanding loans, so ongoing loan interest deductions affect the final value available upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on the account value, which accumulates interest at a rate that may vary monthly, making the interest rate relevant to the final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value depends on the account value, which grows through daily interest credits tied to the current interest rate mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">A higher account value driven by the guaranteed minimum interest rate enhances the cash surrender value, making early surrenders more financially favorable while still subject to surrender charge reductions over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of cash surrender value depends on the account value, which grows at an annual rate of 3.5%, linking back to the interest rate stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on the account value, which itself is subject to variable interest rates depending on account size, making the interest crediting mechanism relevant to determining surrender outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans impact both cash surrender value and death benefit amounts, showing consistent treatment of debt obligations across policy exit events.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">Cash Surrender Value relies on Account Value as its primary source, modifying it by deducting surrender charges and outstanding loans before payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 relies on the existence and application of the Surrender Charge mentioned in fact_sentence_1, showing that the latter provides necessary information for computing the former’s outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value depends on the Account Value, which is built from premiums less a 3% expense charge, making the initial funding process critical to eventual surrender outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value formula depends on current Account Value levels; therefore, any drop leading to a grace period directly impacts potential surrender payouts under the defined conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
