    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes a concrete rate for surrender charges in year 10, which directly informs part of the calculation defined in fact_sentence_1 regarding the deduction from account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="d2bec389-f814-4532-8f19-68d9fc0c9d10">
      <data key="d3">Surrender Charge in Year 10 is lower than in Year 1, illustrating how surrender fees diminish progressively throughout the life of the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases over time</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="be5a6946-58ba-4487-a91b-97d9949ba78f">
      <data key="d3">A lower surrender charge of 2% in year 10 compared to 5% in year 5 indicates a progressive reduction in fees, aligning with the policy’s diminishing surrender costs over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">increased from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in year 10 reflects a cost associated with terminating the policy, directly leading to its cancellation upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="f6b5e972-2fde-453a-98fa-9ea8711ed5fa">
      <data key="d3">The surrender charge decreases from 2% in year 10 to 0% in year 15 or later, reflecting a gradual reduction in penalties over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">decreases to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 2% in year 10 applies when the policyholder chooses to terminate the policy, leading to its cancellation and cessation of coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">The surrender charge in year 10 affects the amount recoverable upon policy lapse, influencing whether an account value exceeds surrender charges when the policy lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 gives a precise figure for the surrender charge in Year 10, which directly feeds into the computation described in fact_sentence_1, where such charges are subtracted from the account value to determine the final cash surrender value.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="733fa6c6-1173-4248-94bb-47741de40661">
      <data key="d3">The lower surrender charge in year 10 compared to year 1 indicates a diminishing penalty for early termination, supporting the idea of reduced fees as the policy ages.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases over time</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in year 10 influences the net cash surrender value, which is reduced not only by this fee but also by any outstanding policy loans that lower the death benefit dollar-for-dollar.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">A surrender charge in Year 10 depends on the Account Value, which is determined by accumulated premiums, fees, and interest as described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 gives a specific instance of a surrender charge at Year 10, reinforcing and concretizing the broader principle stated in fact_sentence_1 about percentage-based fees during the initial 15-year period.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
