    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">The condition regarding suicide within two years relies on knowing how much of the policy's value remains, specifically the Account Value, which is defined in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d3">When an insured dies by suicide within 24 months, the insurer pays only the account value, and this amount does not include any accrued interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20">
      <data key="d3">Suicide within two years limits payout to the account value, while misrepresentation allows the insurer to challenge claims—both apply during the initial underwriting scrutiny window.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="64f378fd-3e2e-4610-87e4-f7c8a0139286">
      <data key="d3">Suicide within two years triggers a restricted payout based on the account value, but this limitation arises because the insurer retains the right to contest the policy’s validity during the initial two-year period.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a scenario where the death benefit is reduced to account value if suicide occurs early, which indirectly affects how cash surrender value might be interpreted in non-surrender contexts, particularly regarding what constitutes final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">exception to rule</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="733fa6c6-1173-4248-94bb-47741de40661">
      <data key="d3">A death benefit reduced to account value in case of suicide mirrors the impact of surrender charges, where actual proceeds are diminished by fees before being disbursed.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">Suicide within two years limits the death benefit to account value, which already excludes any outstanding loan reductions. Thus, the effect of loans is further constrained by this clause.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits effect of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">A suicide-related payout limited to the account value depends on what remains after recurring costs like the cost of insurance have been deducted over time, making prior deductions relevant to the final payout amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The suicide clause limits payout to the account value, meaning that prior deductions like loan interest impact what remains available, indirectly affecting the outcome described in fact_sentence_1 regarding account balance adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences account value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">The suicide-related payout limitation relies on the account value, which grows based on an annual interest rate that may vary monthly, making the actual payout sensitive to these rate changes.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">A suicide-related payout limitation depends on the account value, which is dynamically updated through daily interest crediting based on the current interest rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">The suicide clause limits the death benefit to the account value, making the actual accumulated value—which depends on the credited interest rate—a critical factor in determining the final payout, thus linking back to the guaranteed minimum interest rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">The provision that only the account value is paid upon suicide within two years depends on the account value being calculated based on an annual interest rate of 3.5%, linking back to fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The restriction to paying only the account value in case of early suicide does not affect how interest is credited but limits the final benefit even if higher interest increases the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits benefit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 restricts death benefits to the account value if suicide occurs within two years, which could override standard deduction practices like loan subtraction. However, since the account value already excludes loans, the final payout aligns with what’s stated in fact_sentence_1 regarding net amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to loan</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The suicide clause relies on the precise calculation of Account Value as defined earlier, making the initial explanation critical for interpreting the financial outcome in this scenario.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 restricts death benefits if suicide happens within two years, whereas fact_sentence_1 imposes a fee for surrendering the policy before year 15. Both describe limitations on full payout depending on circumstances surrounding policy exit.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The condition in fact_sentence_2—that only the Account Value is payable on suicide within two years—depends directly on the calculation process outlined in fact_sentence_1, where premiums are reduced by expenses before being added to the Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">If an insured dies by suicide within two years, even during a grace period due to low Account Value, the insurer pays only the Account Value rather than full benefits, making the grace period irrelevant to final payout amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fddbf66a-21bb-4ff2-9852-8051be42bc18" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">excluded from payout under suicide clause</data>
    </edge>
