      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="b2789b32-9b52-4c17-b18d-4c92626235bb">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="01f2bd8a-b7ed-4e67-87fb-df62715441d2">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">When suicide occurs within two years, the account value is paid out without interest, regardless of the standard cash surrender value computation that includes surrender charges and loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">exempt from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">A key consequence of policy surrender—the end of coverage—is relevant because it determines whether certain conditions, such as suicide within two years, trigger modified benefit payouts instead of full death benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">A suicide claim within two years leads to a reduced payout based on account value without interest, reinforcing that such events result in policy termination and loss of future benefits, consistent with surrender terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies termination</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">The exclusion of interest from the account value payment upon suicide death within 24 months clarifies the final payout amount under such circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="64f378fd-3e2e-4610-87e4-f7c8a0139286">
      <data key="d3">Suicide within two years triggers a restricted payout without interest, consistent with the insurer's ability to contest the policy’s validity during the initial contestability period.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">While the Cost of Insurance charge is consistently deducted from the Account Value, in cases of suicide within two years, any accrued interest on that Account Value is forfeited, meaning prior deductions may have less impact due to reduced growth potential.</data>
      <data key="d4">exception to rule</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">While loan interest is typically subtracted monthly from the account value, suicide within two years prevents any interest from being applied to the final payout, overriding standard accumulation rules even if interest was previously accrued.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies conditionally</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">A suicide death within 24 months triggers a rule where no interest is added to the account value, rendering the current interest rate irrelevant for such cases despite its potential variability.</data>
      <data key="d4">contradicts if applied</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The absence of interest credit upon suicide within 24 months contradicts the standard practice of daily interest accumulation, effectively overriding the usual crediting mechanism under exceptional circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">While the 2.0% minimum interest rate ensures baseline growth, its benefits may be nullified in suicide cases within the first two years, where no interest is credited despite the guarantee.</data>
      <data key="d4">exception to guarantee</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">When the insured dies by suicide within 24 months, the absence of accrued interest contradicts the normal application of the 3.5% annual interest rate, effectively nullifying its effect on the settlement amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional exclusion</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">Even though higher account values might earn more interest under standard terms, a suicide claim within two years nullifies any accumulated interest, resulting in a payout equal to the base account value without additional credits.</data>
      <data key="d4">exception to rule</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 limits interest accumulation on the account value in cases of early suicide, which affects the total amount available before deducting loans—a factor considered in fact_sentence_1’s rule about net death benefit computation.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies payout terms</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 restricts interest crediting under specific circumstances involving suicide, fact_sentence_1 establishes the baseline mechanism for Account Value accumulation, making its application contingent on event-based exceptions like those outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional limitation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5242bc64-e720-45f5-b11a-3f7e1500d0e7" target="11c7e060-3470-463f-81cb-576f40036743">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is subject to no interest payment if suicide occurs within 24 months</data>
    </edge>
