    <edge source="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">Insurers have the right to contest claims based on misrepresentation within two years, which applies regardless of whether the policy was surrendered or remains active.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20" target="c17b6902-b6ee-401e-82aa-c2427e58266a">
      <data key="d3">Claims can be contested due to misrepresentation in the first two years, which includes scenarios like suicide where benefits are limited to the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20" target="64f378fd-3e2e-4610-87e4-f7c8a0139286">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 identifies the grounds for contestation (material misrepresentation) within the initial two years, which falls under the broader framework described in fact_sentence_2—that such contests are permitted throughout the two-year contestability period while the individual remains alive.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">If there's material misrepresentation within two years of issuance, the policy may be contested, potentially negating the right to receive the calculated cash surrender value derived from account value, loans, and surrender charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">contradicts if</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">A policy invalidated due to misrepresentation within two years would prevent any death benefit payout, rendering the rule about deducting loans moot.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">If there was material misrepresentation, the insurer can cancel the policy even though the Account Value has been accumulating according to standard formulas involving premiums and charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to risk</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">If a material misrepresentation is found within two years, the policy’s validity may be questioned, potentially invalidating prior premium allocations despite correct application of the 3% fee.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to risk</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="408d21ed-0f24-4d64-b1ef-e8f652db8681" target="adf31acf-2732-44ca-9d60-9d2ebd3c0e20">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">defines issue date for contestability period</data>
    </edge>
