    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">When the account value cannot meet monthly deductions, the insurer sends a notice, initiating a 61-day grace period during which the policy remains active despite financial shortfalls.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">When the account value cannot meet monthly deductions, the insurer notifies the policyholder. This alert precedes the 61-day grace period, during which unresolved shortfalls lead directly to policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">When the account value cannot meet monthly deductions, the insurer notifies the policyholder, potentially leading to non-payment and eventual policy lapse. Upon lapse, any remaining account value beyond surrender charges is automatically refunded.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">Insufficient Account Value to cover the monthly Cost of Insurance charge triggers an automated notification from the insurer, highlighting a failure point in the deduction process.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers warning</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">When the account lacks sufficient funds to absorb the $8.00 monthly administrative charge, the system initiates a notification procedure based on the rule defined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers warning</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">Insufficient Account Value to cover loan interest deductions prompts the insurer to issue a notification, highlighting the importance of maintaining adequate reserves against such mandatory withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers notification</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">Insufficient account value leading to deduction failures depends partly on how effectively interest accrues, which varies based on the current interest rate set monthly.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">Insufficient account value leading to a notification may result from inadequate daily interest accruals, especially if the credited rate is near its guaranteed minimum, affecting overall fund stability.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">If the account value drops due to inadequate growth—potentially influenced by interest rates near the 2.0% minimum—the insurer may issue a notification about insufficient funds, highlighting the importance of the guaranteed rate in sustaining sufficient balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">If the account value drops too low due to poor returns or high fees, even a stable 3.5% interest may not prevent notifications about insufficient funds, meaning the interest rate alone cannot guarantee avoidance of such alerts.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">Insufficient account value leading to deduction failures highlights why variable interest rates matter—lower earnings due to smaller balances may contribute to such shortfalls despite fixed-rate crediting tiers.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Failure to maintain adequate account value triggers warnings, which may lead to increased risk of loan accumulation or lapse—both factors that directly affect the net death benefit paid out.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
