    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a 61-day grace period where policies remain active even if account value cannot meet monthly deductions. This context relies on the existence of an account value, referenced in fact_sentence_1, though the two statements operate independently regarding policy status versus payout calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">Even though the policy may eventually terminate due to surrender, it continues to remain active for 61 days when the account value fails to meet deduction requirements, providing a buffer before coverage ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">delayed by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d">
      <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows continued policy activity after insufficient account value fails to cover deductions, prompting the insurer to issue a notification before lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">If the account value cannot cover monthly deductions, the policy enters a 61-day grace period. After this period expires without adequate premium being paid, the policy lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">If the account value cannot cover monthly deductions, the policy enters a 61-day grace period before lapsing, at which point any excess account value beyond surrender charges is automatically refunded.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a buffer period post-insufficient funding, enabling continuation before lapse, which contextualizes why calculating cash surrender value matters—it determines what is returned if the policy eventually surrenders under such conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="733fa6c6-1173-4248-94bb-47741de40661">
      <data key="d3">A policyholder facing an 8% surrender charge may use the 61-day grace period to replenish the account value before triggering surrender penalties.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows continued policy activity despite insufficient account value, which could result from prior policy loans reducing available funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">If the Account Value fails to cover the monthly Cost of Insurance charge, the policy remains active for 61 days before lapsing, providing a buffer despite the ongoing deduction requirement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">If the account value is too low to cover the $8.00 monthly administrative charge, the policy enters a 61-day grace period before lapsing, allowing continued activity despite non-payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers grace period</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows time for resolving shortfalls caused by loan interest deductions, ensuring policies remain active despite insufficient funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">If the account value drops too low due to inadequate interest crediting (which varies monthly), the policy may enter a 61-day grace period despite ongoing premium obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">If the account value drops too low due to inadequate interest crediting, the policy enters a 61-day grace period, meaning the mechanism described in fact_sentence_1 becomes critical in maintaining sufficient funds to avoid lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period provides temporary financial flexibility when account value falls short of covering deductions, reducing pressure on maintaining high returns—but still relies on the guaranteed 2.0% minimum interest to prevent rapid depletion.</data>
      <data key="d4">supprts</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">If the account value drops too low to meet monthly deductions, the policy enters a 61-day grace period, making the effective growth rate critical—especially since interest is credited daily based on the 3.5% annual rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">If the account value drops too low due to lower-than-expected interest accruals, it may trigger the 61-day grace period before lapse, making interest crediting conditions relevant to policy continuation.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">A death benefit is adjusted downward by any existing policy loans, so maintaining the policy through the 61-day grace period helps preserve the full account value and prevents premature termination that could limit claimable funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">A sufficient Account Value ensures timely payment of monthly deductions; otherwise, the policy enters a 61-day grace period while still maintaining coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables grace period</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">If a policyholder surrenders within the first 15 years, a percentage-based surrender charge applies; however, if the account lacks sufficient funds to sustain payments, the 61-day grace period may delay surrender decisions, possibly influencing whether such fees are incurred.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">If the Account Value becomes too low to cover monthly deductions, the policy enters a 61-day grace period, meaning no further premium allocations occur until resolution—even though initial premiums were subject to a 3% charge before being added.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states the policy remains active during the 61-day grace period, clarifying the consequence described in fact_sentence_1 where falling Account Value initiates the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
