    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="0155c9de-0b82-477a-9ec7-27cf965dc575">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums within 61 days leads to policy lapse, an alternative path to termination that differs from voluntary surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="afcce2ca-db53-4aa4-8a56-3863abb45a24">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums within 61 days causes the policy to lapse, terminating coverage. This outcome aligns with what occurs upon surrender, though triggered differently.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative cause</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay sufficient premium within 61 days causes the policy to lapse. This outcome depends on prior insufficiency in account value that triggered the initial notification.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">Failure to receive sufficient premium within 61 days causes the policy to lapse, but only after an initial grace period allows continued activity when account value is low.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a">
      <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid within the 61-day grace period, the policy lapses, leading to an automatic payout of any remaining account value beyond surrender charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the timeline leading to policy lapse if premiums are not paid, which could prevent access to the cash surrender value defined in fact_sentence_1 unless action is taken before expiration.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="733fa6c6-1173-4248-94bb-47741de40661">
      <data key="d3">Failure to meet premium obligations within 61 days causes policy lapse, eliminating future surrender opportunities and rendering the initial 8% surrender charge irrelevant since no formal surrender occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">A policy lapse due to unpaid premiums halts future cost of insurance deductions, rendering them irrelevant once coverage ceases.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse after 61 days, which could result in loss of accumulated interest gains tied to the changing annual rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums within 61 days causes policy lapse, halting future interest credits even if the current rate remains favorable.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without immediate lapse, giving the guaranteed interest rate more opportunity to grow the account balance toward sustaining coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, eliminating the possibility of a death benefit payout, thus making the deduction of loan balances from such a benefit moot unless the policy is surrendered prior to lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">A lack of sufficient premium within 61 days causes policy lapse, which affects the final Account Value available at termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">A policy that fails to receive adequate premiums within 61 days lapses, preventing any future surrender and thus nullifying the applicability of surrender charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents surrender</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">Failure to maintain adequate premium contributions within 61 days undermines the accumulation mechanism where premiums are reduced by a 3% fee before adding to the Account Value.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period activates when the account value cannot cover ongoing charges, providing temporary protection against immediate lapse. This grace period exists specifically to prevent termination unless adequate premium remains unpaid beyond its duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bb474e81-72f2-435d-bf5d-be882ffc96ac" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">enforces policy lapse after grace period</data>
    </edge>
