    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="ca4ca85e-d0c7-4f15-93d4-03a1cb8f9b19">
      <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, the refundable amount is determined by subtracting surrender charges from the account value. This outcome relies directly on the Cash Surrender Value being defined as Account Value minus surrender charges and loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="d2bec389-f814-4532-8f19-68d9fc0c9d10">
      <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, any surplus account value after deducting surrender charges is returned automatically, meaning the initial surrender charge rate influences the final payout outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="be5a6946-58ba-4487-a91b-97d9949ba78f">
      <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, any surplus account value beyond surrender charges is refunded automatically, making the specific surrender charge level relevant to determining the actual payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="ddfa898f-d3e4-4e89-9fe3-ece66a9197ed">
      <data key="d3">If the account value exceeds surrender charges at lapse, the specific charge percentage (like 2%) determines how much remains available for payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="f6b5e972-2fde-453a-98fa-9ea8711ed5fa">
      <data key="d3">A policy’s automatic refund of surplus account value at lapse depends on surrender charges being eliminated, such as in year 15 or later when they reach 0%.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="70a90dda-a504-430c-b48f-97a62091716e">
      <data key="d3">After a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, any remaining account value above surrender charges is returned automatically, which occurs following the 61-day grace period mentioned earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="9e69c3b1-81e7-420c-93e4-41aab51bc29d">
      <data key="d3">After a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, any surplus account value over surrender charges is returned automatically. This outcome could have been preceded by a notice sent when the account value was too low to sustain deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="d24747c1-d663-4439-9454-0b5bd8f1185c">
      <data key="d3">An automatic payout of surplus account value occurs upon policy lapse, which happens specifically when premiums remain unpaid past the 61-day grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="e467f66f-8ebe-41fd-8e9c-a879c062996c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies the outcome of policy lapse—the return of surplus account value after deducting surrender charges—which aligns with and provides practical application for the theoretical framework outlined in fact_sentence_1 regarding cash surrender calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="733fa6c6-1173-4248-94bb-47741de40661">
      <data key="d3">If a policyholder lets the policy lapse, the portion of the account value not offset by the 8% surrender charge in year one is automatically refunded, meaning the high early surrender cost limits recoverable amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="ce5368c1-45d3-4d18-a2cd-ed25bfce9ea9">
      <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, any remaining account value after surrender charges is returned; however, prior policy loans diminish this amount since they reduce the effective account value available for distribution.</data>
      <data key="d4">influenced by loans</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="d2d7f644-175d-4fe0-ae25-131e657d096a">
      <data key="d3">The automatic return of surplus account value upon lapse depends on the accumulated impact of recurring costs like the monthly insurance charge, making the timing and magnitude of those deductions relevant to the final settlement.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="b3a92b86-1b3f-437a-94f2-971cc4413b8a">
      <data key="d3">A higher account value due to reduced deductions may increase the refundable amount upon lapse, but the administrative fee has no direct impact on the lapse process or eligibility for return of surplus funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="40116a52-d516-4b17-8b5c-41312619c88e">
      <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, the remaining Account Value after surrender charges includes adjustments for prior loan interest deductions, meaning earlier interest payments impact the final refundable amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="2e4a0b31-0a77-4786-b43e-9df3c67b4a3a">
      <data key="d3">The automatic refund of surplus account value upon lapse depends on the accumulated value driven by the prevailing interest rate, making the timing and level of interest critical to the final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="de1c9695-ef86-44d3-817c-e20ff49543a7">
      <data key="d3">The refundable amount upon lapse depends on the account value, which accumulates through daily interest credits based on the current interest rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="5055565e-cbfe-44d3-be16-afa1d965e079">
      <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, the accumulated account value—enhanced by the guaranteed minimum 2.0% annual interest—is partially offset by surrender charges before being paid out to the holder.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="ceb49223-6965-4e32-9d3a-c537fbfff452">
      <data key="d3">A higher account value resulting from the 3.5% annual interest rate enhances the amount payable upon policy lapse, making the interest rate relevant to the outcome described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="53be9ad3-d3ad-4925-9bb5-c12ac65a8012">
      <data key="d3">The automatic refund of surplus account value upon lapse depends on the total account value, which accumulates through interest credits that vary by account size.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="aa42baaa-8e4d-4623-89b2-4f42a9c006fa">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans affect not just death benefit payouts but also the amount recoverable upon lapse, meaning loan balances diminish returns regardless of whether the trigger is death or policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="b74a2cf6-0be5-410f-8b0b-75a035485c22">
      <data key="d3">The outcome of a policy lapse—returning surplus Account Value after surrender charges—is contingent on knowing how Account Value itself is defined and accumulated.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="d59f0cd9-1a58-404b-85a4-9cde309d52b8">
      <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, any surplus in account value after subtracting surrender charges is refunded—this outcome depends on the existence and magnitude of those charges, as defined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="0a744329-f2e4-42aa-90c7-0552ff65e5c1">
      <data key="d3">The automatic refund of excess Account Value at lapse assumes prior accumulation via premium allocations net of fees, directly relying on the process described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="31c00839-d964-44d5-8027-45be3fef034a" target="5e1c407b-5a34-46a9-a8c2-c1e5dc597284">
      <data key="d3">A policy entering a 61-day grace period due to insufficient account value ultimately risks lapsing, at which point any remaining account value above surrender charges is automatically returned to the policyholder.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
